{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities","id":849897,"title":"Angelic Form Abilities?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T15:21:43-07:00","id":849897,"title":"Angelic Form Abilities?","content":"Hey again guys, how are you? After reading Children of a Killer God again, something occurred to to me: It does not talk about angels utilizing form abilities whatsoever. While I realize chapter space limitations were likely the reason; the fact that there isn't even a side box addressing the issue really puzzled me. Angels have them, both the core book and players guide mention that angels do indeed possess form abilities like demons, but the st guide doesn't even give a blurb how form abilities differ from their less powerful demonic versions. I feel like this must be rectified. So, what are you guys' thoughts on angelic form parts and their functions? I would appreciate your thoughts and even some homebrewed examples of modified or wholecloth form abilities if you all have the time. Thanks, and have a wonderful day!<br /> <br /> And thanks to Vent0, all the form abilities I have built up to this point have been compiled into a neat and tidy google document for a greater ease of viewing: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O_HIomzEMusF-3-0KCWuaZh_KWhkC959745mF4-tWQw/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.rdyee771nlyl\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.rdyee771nlyl</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:24:01-07:00","id":849898,"title":"","content":"They....don't differ?<br /> <br /> Seems kind of obvious to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:34:25-07:00","id":849902,"title":"","content":"I have thought of one myself; I hope you enjoy them!<br /> <br /> <b>Material Conversion System ( Angelic Process)</b><br /> Some angels are deployed on harvesting or recycling missions to acquire or require resources for the Machine. With this in built ability, an angel is able to convert rare materials or physical pieces of Infrastructure back into usable fuel for the God-Machine, as well as recharging their own energy reserves.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The Angel's midsection has been reprocessed into a matter/energy converter. Perhaps it resembles a glass fronted furnace what burns away physical matter, or a chemical vat filled with etheric chemicals, or even just a highly efficient multi chambered stomach.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel can swallow physical matter, and by doing so converts it into essence. The angel rolls it's Rank + Resistance trait - the swallowed object's Durability. Success means the the ingested object is rapidly broken down, suffering one point of aggravated damage per turn until completely destroyed. The angel in return gains one point of essence equal to each point of durability the consumed object possesses. Failing the roll causes the angel to forcibly regurgitate the object, though they are free to attempt to break it down again on their next turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-23-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:38:13-07:00","id":849903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849898#post849898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They....don't differ?<br /> <br /> Seems kind of obvious to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them very much do, according to descriptions for demonic form abilities. Multiple Images for example states that angels who possess it can make copies of themselves that are capable to taking physical action, while the demonic version creates merely highly realistic illusions/holograms. So there are some differences for at least some form abilities. Now for others, I agree that they probably do not differ much or at all, like Armored Plates or Rivet Arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-19-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:08:03-07:00","id":849915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849903#post849903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of them very much do, according to descriptions for demonic form abilities. Multiple Images for example states that angels who possess it can make copies of themselves that are capable to taking physical action, while the demonic version creates merely highly realistic illusions/holograms. So there are some differences for at least some form abilities. Now for others, I agree that they probably do not differ much or at all, like Armored Plates or Rivet Arm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Considering Angels are still plugged into the God Machine and that the fall is rather traumatic on the Unchained it could also just be that the system doesn't work as well for the Unchained who have it. Like if part of multiple image system operated by using the connection to the GM as external hardware then an Angel would be able to pull off more just because no demon has the needed processing power. Or the system tends to get damaged during a fall. That being said I would not be opposed to the idea of evolved tech on Angels with the idea that well upgrades have been made to the system since you fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:14:16-07:00","id":849919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849915#post849915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily. Considering Angels are still plugged into the God Machine and that the fall is rather traumatic on the Unchained it could also just be that the system doesn't work as well for the Unchained who have it. Like if part of multiple image system operated by using the connection to the GM as external hardware then an Angel would be able to pull off more just because no demon has the needed processing power. Or the system tends to get damaged during a fall. That being said I would not be opposed to the idea of evolved tech on Angels with the idea that well upgrades have been made to the system since you fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still means that the utilization of their systems is different, even if it is because the God-Machine provides greater processing/ technical capability. Now I agree with angels having access to higher &quot;tiers&quot; of form abilities or more optimized versions of existing pieces, that would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:28:20-07:00","id":849972,"title":"","content":"I've used form abilities for angels, I just give them the same number as a demon (4,3,2,1), 1 essence let's them manifest (Rank) form abilities at a time, or go full angelic form, at the cost of dropping any pretense of being inconspicuous. Between Influences, Incepts and Numina, angels have enough meat that they don't need more powerful form abilities, though if you want to do a plot thread in your chronicle about the G-M machine developing new and superior form abilities...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:32:52-07:00","id":849973,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering about how to run the idea of an Angelic Form. Personally, I think that with everything else they've got going for them, even the maximum demon spread is a lot. I've run it as their natural abilities that pop out when they drop Mortal Mask.<br /> <br /> I'm curious, how do you guys run Angelic Cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:42:11-07:00","id":850000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849972#post849972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used form abilities for angels, I just give them the same number as a demon (4,3,2,1)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a nitpick, it's 3/2/1/1 and it only ever gets to 4/3/1/2 without Terrible Form, Advance Form, or High Tolerance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T00:11:02-07:00","id":850047,"title":"","content":"Assuming that an Angel's form powers are stronger than those of a Demon's does up te ante if you give them said powers in the process. And it'd be pretty interesting to see write-ups for the different form powers in the hands of an Angel, where applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:17:06-07:00","id":850175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849972#post849972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used form abilities for angels, I just give them the same number as a demon (4,3,2,1), 1 essence let's them manifest (Rank) form abilities at a time, or go full angelic form, at the cost of dropping any pretense of being inconspicuous. Between Influences, Incepts and Numina, angels have enough meat that they don't need more powerful form abilities, though if you want to do a plot thread in your chronicle about the G-M machine developing new and superior form abilities...</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with Satch that the spread is a little odd with how numbers go, but it doesn't bother me- I would imagine angels would naturally have more bits anyway, they just get sheared off when the Fall happens XD. And I also agree that with their Incepts, Influences, and Numina do cover for a lot of things form abilities offer, sometimes you still need those extra arms or healing protocols, it saves Essence for more important functions after all.<br /> <br /> .. And I also agree in finding the concept of the God-Machine outfitting it's units with powerful &quot;next gen&quot; form abilities as it were.. it's a great story hook to demonstrate just how more advanced/cutting edge angels can be compared to their jury-rigged fallen cousins. Huh would you look at that, lots of agreements from me today XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:20:33-07:00","id":850176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850000#post850000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a nitpick, it's 3/2/1/1 and it only ever gets to 4/3/1/2 without Terrible Form, Advance Form, or High Tolerance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always a rare honor to see you posting in threads I start, even if it is to clarify things. I confess, it's a &quot;senpai noticed&quot; moment even if it doesn't directly involve me XD. I do have to ask, what exactly was High Tolerance again? I vaguely remember reading it, but for the life of me can't remember what it entails. Having said that, how do you handle Form Abilities Satch? I'm curious to know what you do with them concerning angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:21:23-07:00","id":850177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850047#post850047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that an Angel's form powers are stronger than those of a Demon's does up te ante if you give them said powers in the process. And it'd be pretty interesting to see write-ups for the different form powers in the hands of an Angel, where applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>agreed, I was hoping to see the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:25:16-07:00","id":850178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=849973#post849973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering about how to run the idea of an Angelic Form. Personally, I think that with everything else they've got going for them, even the maximum demon spread is a lot. I've run it as their natural abilities that pop out when they drop Mortal Mask.<br /> <br /> I'm curious, how do you guys run Angelic Cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally run Angelic Cover much like normal Cover, though under normal circumstances I do not bother with doing compromise rolls. I figure the God-Machine can patch their Covers on the fly should a potential compromise occur, so their identities are rarely in danger under normal circumstances. That doesn't mean their Covers can't fray; it's just much harder for them to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:14:39-07:00","id":850197,"title":"","content":"I always figured angelic form abilities were covered by a combination of numina, influences and general storyteller fudgery. They're like embeds. They're there, but Angels just sort of use them organically with no fanfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:27:51-07:00","id":850205,"title":"","content":"I find myself agreeing with Elfive. The books never seemed to bring up the thought of Angels' forms being represented with the same mechanical abstractions as Demonic Form, so I always saw those traits as included in the systems that normally define them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-20-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:29:30-07:00","id":850206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850197#post850197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured angelic form abilities were covered by a combination of numina, influences and general storyteller fudgery. They're like embeds. They're there, but Angels just sort of use them organically with no fanfare.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely one way to go about it. I personally don't like doing that, but it's a viable way to cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T13:18:01-07:00","id":850228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850000#post850000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a nitpick, it's 3/2/1/1 and it only ever gets to 4/3/1/2 without Terrible Form, Advance Form, or High Tolerance.</div> </div> </div> </div>::checks the DTD book, sees that Satchel is correct::<br /> Huh, nuts. Well, that does explain why the last two angels were such beasts...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850175#post850175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do agree with Satch that the spread is a little odd with how numbers go, but it doesn't bother me- I would imagine angels would naturally have more bits anyway, they just get sheared off when the Fall happens XD. And I also agree that with their Incepts, Influences, and Numina do cover for a lot of things form abilities offer, sometimes you still need those extra arms or healing protocols, it saves Essence for more important functions after all.<br /> <br /> .. And I also agree in finding the concept of the God-Machine outfitting it's units with powerful &quot;next gen&quot; form abilities as it were.. it's a great story hook to demonstrate just how more advanced/cutting edge angels can be compared to their jury-rigged fallen cousins. Huh would you look at that, lots of agreements from me today XD</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd recommend against giving an angel extra form abilities unless you deem that they have Terrible Form/Advanced Form. The three form abilities that demons get from increasing their Primum represent the Unchained surpassing the designs to the G-m. It's a small point, but one that reinforces the game's theme.<br /> <br /> From the description of Cover on page 111 of DtD, it looks like angels experience cover in a different way: Logistical and Concealment Infrastructure is constantly update/maintaining and repairing it. Demons have to repair and maintain their own cover. Consider how a college student who has a trust fund and daddy's credit card thinks about money versus one who's on a work-scholarship.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:39:29-07:00","id":850282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850176#post850176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have to ask, what exactly was High Tolerance again? I vaguely remember reading it, but for the life of me can't remember what it entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Tolerance lets you incorporate a form gadget without giving up one of your abilities to make space for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having said that, how do you handle Form Abilities Satch? I'm curious to know what you do with them concerning angels. </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the same as Elfive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:49:43-07:00","id":850631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850282#post850282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Tolerance lets you incorporate a form gadget without giving up one of your abilities to make space for it.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the same as Elfive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thank you then.<br /> <br /> Aww... well that was less exciting than I hoped/expected","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:00:13-07:00","id":850639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850228#post850228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd recommend against giving an angel extra form abilities unless you deem that they have Terrible Form/Advanced Form. The three form abilities that demons get from increasing their Primum represent the Unchained surpassing the designs to the G-m. It's a small point, but one that reinforces the game's theme.<br /> <br /> From the description of Cover on page 111 of DtD, it looks like angels experience cover in a different way: Logistical and Concealment Infrastructure is constantly update/maintaining and repairing it. Demons have to repair and maintain their own cover. Consider how a college student who has a trust fund and daddy's credit card thinks about money versus one who's on a work-scholarship.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be more specific, it does represent them surpassing the original design of the Machine. But That doesn't mean that other, more powerful angels do not possess additional form abilities, without Terrible form/Advanced form ( I don't think they require these merits personally, I merely think it represents what is left of the demon, some being luckier to retain more bits and bobs than others). Hence why I earlier said that I imagined that the Fall burns away said additions that an angel may have, if indeed they did. Demons do lose parts doing the Fall after all XD<br /> <br /> Hey, I resemble that remark about scholarships.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-21-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T22:04:19-07:00","id":853899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=850205#post850205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself agreeing with Elfive. The books never seemed to bring up the thought of Angels' forms being represented with the same mechanical abstractions as Demonic Form, so I always saw those traits as included in the systems that normally define them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. One of my biggest struggles running DtD has been making angels more than just spirits that show up when player flubs a compromise roll. As is, angels have a very limited budget of Numina (3 per rank) and most of their dice pools are pretty limited until they hit rank three, or start spending essence to boost them, which can get expensive.<br /> <br /> There's something visceral about talking to a guy, thinking he's just a guy, then having his hand turn into a drill of liquid metal and starting to spit acid... that gets a player's attention in a way that a Numen or an Influence just doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 03-27-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T03:05:26-07:00","id":853955,"title":"","content":"You're looking at it the wrong way. Turning his hand into a drill and spitting acid <i>are </i>numina. Or at least the latter is. Definitely works as an application of blast. The first one doesn't really need a power associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:58:44-07:00","id":855269,"title":"","content":"Maybe so... But I sort of have to ask this question: If that is the case.. Why would they translate into demonic form abilities? Embeds effectively replace numina after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:24:10-07:00","id":855290,"title":"","content":"Embeds most certainly do not replace numina. Page 123 of Demon states, &quot;Angels do not make conscious effort to use Embeds, they are able to do so simply as part of their missions.&quot; A numen is very much a concious power that one chooses to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:39:32-07:00","id":855326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855290#post855290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embeds most certainly do not replace numina. Page 123 of Demon states, &amp;quot;Angels do not make conscious effort to use Embeds, they are able to do so simply as part of their missions.&amp;quot; A numen is very much a concious power that one chooses to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand me. Embeds take place of Numina for a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:42:42-07:00","id":855330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=853899#post853899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. One of my biggest struggles running DtD has been making angels more than just spirits that show up when player flubs a compromise roll. As is, angels have a very limited budget of Numina (3 per rank) and most of their dice pools are pretty limited until they hit rank three, or start spending essence to boost them, which can get expensive.<br /> <br /> There's something visceral about talking to a guy, thinking he's just a guy, then having his hand turn into a drill of liquid metal and starting to spit acid... that gets a player's attention in a way that a Numen or an Influence just doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even setting aside Elfive's point about Acid Spit = Blast, I'm not sure why an Angel can't do that in the rules as is. Just have drills of liquid metal and acidic spit as part of the Angel's physical description. Anything above a Rank 1 Angel probably has a dice pool big enough to justify it.<br /> <br /> As for only showing up when someone flubs a Compromise Roll, what about the Angels out and about on missions unrelated to Demons? I would call such beings as some of the most valuable assets in a Demon Storyteller's arsenal. Adding a Psychopomp or Messenger Angel who doesn't give a fig about worming out Demons lets you have scenes other than, &quot;An Angel appears, fight/flee!&quot; and Angels other than the Destroyer Archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:53:27-07:00","id":855340,"title":"","content":"Well aside from acidic spit being far more dangerous than Blast.. You have a point. And I think that some people are getting too caught up on the &quot;why should angels possess distinct form abilities&quot; bit, which while valid.. It sort of wasnt what i was looking for originally haha. Now dont get me wrong, it is very enlightening, I just had been hoping people would of jumped on the bandwagon of creativity.. But what can you do? XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:57:42-07:00","id":855344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855326#post855326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You misunderstand me. Embeds take place of Numina for a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> RAW, demons Embeds and Demonic form together cover the previous Angels: Numina, Influences, Manifestations, General Abilites (as Azahul says above, just describe the angel as having drill hands is mechanically represented by their large attack pool), being connected to the God-Machine, connecting with Infaustructure and the ability to have the required skills needed for a mission. There isn't a 1 to 1 comparison of any of their powers to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:06:57-07:00","id":855354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855344#post855344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RAW, demons Embeds and Demonic form together cover the previous Angels: Numina, Influences, Manifestations, General Abilites (as Azahul says above, just describe the angel as having drill hands is mechanically represented by their large attack pool), being connected to the God-Machine, connecting with Infaustructure and the ability to have the required skills needed for a mission. There isn't a 1 to 1 comparison of any of their powers to the other.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, you can absolutely do that.. But it isnt very interesting or satisfying to me thematically. It works perfectly fine mechanically however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:26:11-07:00","id":855372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855340#post855340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well aside from acidic spit being far more dangerous than Blast.. You have a point. And I think that some people are getting too caught up on the &quot;why should angels possess distinct form abilities&quot; bit, which while valid.. It sort of wasnt what i was looking for originally haha. Now dont get me wrong, it is very enlightening, I just had been hoping people would of jumped on the bandwagon of creativity.. But what can you do? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure Acidic Spit is that much weaker than Blast. It's, what, a 0A weapon? Blast, with some Essence expenditure, can be a 1L to 5L weapon (much, much higher with Incepts). In most scenarios involving anything that isn't undead, an extra point of lethal damage will be better than aggravated damage. It's not like the target is capable of fighting back after being maxed out on either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:50:31-07:00","id":855421,"title":"","content":"Yeah, never forget the boost provided by the right combination of Incepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:36:34-07:00","id":855486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855372#post855372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure Acidic Spit is that much weaker than Blast. It's, what, a 0A weapon? Blast, with some Essence expenditure, can be a 1L to 5L weapon (much, much higher with Incepts). In most scenarios involving anything that isn't undead, an extra point of lethal damage will be better than aggravated damage. It's not like the target is capable of fighting back after being maxed out on either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said acidic spit was more dangerous than Blast, not weaker lol. And against humans or supernatural beings that cannot properly deal with lethal damage, absolutely. But for tougher creatures like Uratha, Sin-eaters, spirits, or indeed angels or other demons, i would take an ability or weapon that deals aggravated damage over lethal if given the choice, even with the benefits of Incepts, which are really only game breaking at rank 3 or higher. And for undead.. I agree! You hold on tight to your aggro damage and never let go XD.<br /> <br /> Also unless it was changed, I still believe aggravated damage causes Essence loss...now shoukd you be cornered by a hunter angel, that proves invaluable in my books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-30-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:49:32-07:00","id":855489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855421#post855421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, never forget the boost provided by the right combination of Incepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I never do, having said that, Incept usage is immensely situational for angels... Unless they are close to Falling.. Then I have them use Incepts willy nilly XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:29:19-07:00","id":855516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855486#post855486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said acidic spit was more dangerous than Blast, not weaker lol. And against humans or supernatural beings that cannot properly deal with lethal damage, absolutely. But for tougher creatures like Uratha, Sin-eaters, spirits, or indeed angels or other demons, i would take an ability or weapon that deals aggravated damage over lethal if given the choice, even with the benefits of Incepts, which are really only game breaking at rank 3 or higher. And for undead.. I agree! You hold on tight to your aggro damage and never let go XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the scenario we are really looking at here is usually going to be Angel (as the Storyteller) versus the Demon (controlled by the player who &quot;feels&quot; the difference between Acid Spit and Blast). And I do kind of disagree with the notion that Demons can deal with lethal better than Aggravated. For most Demons, lethal damage is about as dangerous as it is for humans.<br /> <br /> You could also make the Blast attack deal aggravated damage and/or corrode armour in the same manner as the form power. Hey look, I can make creative suggestions too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:50:09-07:00","id":855520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855330#post855330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for only showing up when someone flubs a Compromise Roll, what about the Angels out and about on missions unrelated to Demons? I would call such beings as some of the most valuable assets in a Demon Storyteller's arsenal. Adding a Psychopomp or Messenger Angel who doesn't give a fig about worming out Demons lets you have scenes other than, &quot;An Angel appears, fight/flee!&quot; and Angels other than the Destroyer Archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I was using hyperbole to express my frustration with angels becoming mooks, not describing how they show up in a chronicle. <br /> <br /> Critical to the theme of DtD, and to any espionage fiction, is the fear of being caught, of having the protective lie of cover (or Cover) stripped away from you.<br /> <br /> Angels are the manifestation of this fear in DtD. The threat of angels has to have teeth, dealing with angles has to be a source of tension. Angels have to <i>scare</i> the players, no matter what the programming and operational parameters of the angels in question, and no matter what Rank the angel is. In-game fiction has demons <i>terrified</i> of angels. Mechanically... this isn't always been represented in play, especially as players climbed in power. A demon with enough xp can eat a Rank 1 or 2 angel alive, especially if the demon in questions is willing to Go Loud, which is more of an option once they have Burn covers that they aren't as invested in as their main Covers.<br /> <br /> My personal experience has been that angels with form abilities, even rank 2-3 angels, make a stronger impression on my players than ones where the form abilities are mechanically abstracted. In addition, it's helped me portray angels as materially different from other ephemeral beings, and describe the bio-mechanical horror lurking underneath a human mask.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:22:36-07:00","id":855535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855520#post855520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My apologies, I was using hyperbole to express my frustration with angels becoming mooks, not describing how they show up in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Critical to the theme of DtD, and to any espionage fiction, is the fear of being caught, of having the protective lie of cover (or Cover) stripped away from you.<br /> <br /> Angels are the manifestation of this fear in DtD. The threat of angels has to have teeth, dealing with angles has to be a source of tension. Angels have to <i>scare</i> the players, no matter what the programming and operational parameters of the angels in question, and no matter what Rank the angel is. In-game fiction has demons <i>terrified</i> of angels. Mechanically... this isn't always been represented in play, especially as players climbed in power. A demon with enough xp can eat a Rank 1 or 2 angel alive, especially if the demon in questions is willing to Go Loud, which is more of an option once they have Burn covers that they aren't as invested in as their main Covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. I've had the total opposite experience. My group is terrified of Angels as written. A few members of the group have brought up the fact that they actually resent the fact that, from their perspective, they have basically no way to beat an Angel in a fight. Let's remember that a Demon can't even touch an Angel without either knowing its Bane or the Angel using the Materialise Manifestation (popularly referred to in my group as &quot;The GM's going easy on us&quot;). There is the only one power in the whole of Demon that allows a Demon to force a straight an Angel out of Twilight for a straight fight, Reality Enforcement. Even it is not quite foolproof as it tends to require the Demon to get the drop on the Angel or for the Angel to be a melee combatant. Then there is the sheer strength of Numen. Awe, Rapture, and Strike Blind are all nasty things to throw at a Demon who isn't ready for them. The Possess Manifestation is basically an automatic win if you can contrive a way to stick the Open Condition on a player. Or just use the Image Manifestation effect and throw Blasts at the Demons who are helpless to touch you until they keel over.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 Angels are, admittedly, a bit on the weak side. I only have one written for my Chronicle, and I have it designed as something barely above an Imperative. But my players feel that any Angel in the Rank 2+ range is something they should avoid rather than fight if at all possible. Planning to fight an Angel is invariably a big, big deal for them, and something that will require the resources of the entire group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855520#post855520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal experience has been that angels with form abilities, even rank 2-3 angels, make a stronger impression on my players than ones where the form abilities are mechanically abstracted. In addition, it's helped me portray angels as materially different from other ephemeral beings, and describe the bio-mechanical horror lurking underneath a human mask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that I do give my Angels weapons and armour, sometimes fluffed as &quot;natural weapons&quot;, when it makes sense for them to have it. So it's not entirely a bare knuckle fight. And I certainly don't shy away from using descriptions (or pictures) of the Angelic form to ram home the biomechanical horror side of things. I just haven't had much need for any kind of additional game mechanics beyond the Ephemeral Being rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T02:10:19-07:00","id":855588,"title":"","content":"A machine gun is an entirely acceptable manifestation of Blast. So is a flamethrower. Drain could take the form of a large hypodermic needle. It's not that Angels don't have form abilities, but rather that numina and the like <i>are </i>form abilities geared to ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:58:03-07:00","id":855979,"title":"","content":"That is viable too, and before I had this epiphany I would do just that. At the same time, like Westmer I have found the inclusion of form abilities does add a sense of depth to angels that sets them apart from other ephemeral entities for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:02:23-07:00","id":855983,"title":"","content":"How can they tell the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:12:49-07:00","id":855990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855983#post855983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can they tell the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I distinctly describe how their parts interact with the world around them, and the players recognize them as form abilities, either they have or those their friends possess, and they really like how it shows how similar angels and demons still are, despite how different they have become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:18:29-07:00","id":855995,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think the problem is that you apparently <i>weren't</i> doing that with numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:46:08-07:00","id":856024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855995#post855995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think the problem is that you apparently <i>weren't</i> doing that with numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it isnt your place to consider it a &quot;problem&quot; my friend. I do not consider your way to be a storytellling problem, so I respectfully ask you to do the same. Its merely a difference in mechanical and thematic preference. Now that we have that out of the way, i did use numina like that in the beginning, I just found it unsatisfying personally.. So I started using form abilities. The fact that my players enjoyed it being a nice bonus that was incentive for me to keep using form abilities for angels didnt hurt either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-30-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:49:48-07:00","id":856026,"title":"","content":"Eh, whatever works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:56:11-07:00","id":856031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=855516#post855516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the scenario we are really looking at here is usually going to be Angel (as the Storyteller) versus the Demon (controlled by the player who &quot;feels&quot; the difference between Acid Spit and Blast). And I do kind of disagree with the notion that Demons can deal with lethal better than Aggravated. For most Demons, lethal damage is about as dangerous as it is for humans.<br /> <br /> You could also make the Blast attack deal aggravated damage and/or corrode armour in the same manner as the form power. Hey look, I can make creative suggestions too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, normally you are right. The only argument I can make on that point concerning damage would be the Just Bruised Embed is somewhat common, and that does up survivability a good deal, along with some demons possessing Wound Healing are also capable of walking away from attacks dealing lethal damage much more easily than humans. Neither are universal traits, true, but both are worth mentioning when describing the toughness of the Unchained as a whole lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:10:04-07:00","id":856034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856026#post856026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, whatever works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad we agree lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:17:14-07:00","id":856039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856026#post856026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, whatever works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm happy to see the forums are posting my responses more than once haha.. Or not since i just edited this one XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-30-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:06:39-07:00","id":856057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856031#post856031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, normally you are right. The only argument I can make on that point concerning damage would be the Just Bruised Embed is somewhat common, and that does up survivability a good deal, along with some demons possessing Wound Healing are also capable of walking away from attacks dealing lethal damage much more easily than humans. Neither are universal traits, true, but both are worth mentioning when describing the toughness of the Unchained as a whole lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wound Healing is where the difference really matters. To a character who only has Just Bruised they're going to die just the same if they fill up on lethal or aggravated damage even if it is only happening one dot at a time. So that's one single Process, at its best in conjunction with an Embed. There is a big difference between &quot;Demons can deal with lethal more easily than Aggravated damage&quot; and &quot;one specific character build can deal with lethal damage more easily than Aggravated damage if they're willing to risk Compromise&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, personally, I like the fact that Numina and Influences are subtly different mechanically to Form Powers and Embeds, as I think it helps to ram home the differences between Angels and Demons rather than the similarities. For all that one originated from the other, they are very, very different beings metaphysically. And there's also the fact that my players already feel so utterly overwhelmed by Angels that giving the Angels even more powers seems kinda mean.<br /> <br /> (Seriously, I am really, really curious as to how Agentwestmer's group got into a situation wherein Angels feel like &quot;mooks&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:42:41-07:00","id":856243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856057#post856057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wound Healing is where the difference really matters. To a character who only has Just Bruised they're going to die just the same if they fill up on lethal or aggravated damage even if it is only happening one dot at a time. So that's one single Process, at its best in conjunction with an Embed. There is a big difference between &quot;Demons can deal with lethal more easily than Aggravated damage&quot; and &quot;one specific character build can deal with lethal damage more easily than Aggravated damage if they're willing to risk Compromise&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, personally, I like the fact that Numina and Influences are subtly different mechanically to Form Powers and Embeds, as I think it helps to ram home the differences between Angels and Demons rather than the similarities. For all that one originated from the other, they are very, very different beings metaphysically. And there's also the fact that my players already feel so utterly overwhelmed by Angels that giving the Angels even more powers seems kinda mean.<br /> <br /> (Seriously, I am really, really curious as to how Agentwestmer's group got into a situation wherein Angels feel like &quot;mooks&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a bit more wide spread than a singular character build, but you have a point, I admit.<br /> <br /> They are very different,but it isnt the differences that frighten me or a couple of my players. To us, what makes angels so scary, in part, is the fact that they are more clever and subversive than many others give them credit for.. And the fact they represent everything demons were and what they could possibly be again... That is what is frightening.<br /> <br /> And i dunno how that happened, Like you my angels are not the sort of things you just fight.. They are brutal warriors who are not just dangerous because of their strength power but also due to their intelligence and cunning. Not only that, being ephemeral, they are nearly impossible to destroy. So while they have defeated one angel and driven off a couple others... They haven't killed any.<br /> <br /> And fixed lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 03-31-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:02:16-07:00","id":856736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856057#post856057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And there's also the fact that my players already feel so utterly overwhelmed by Angels that giving the Angels even more powers seems kinda mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, when you take Numina, Manifestations, and Incepts into account, it is very mean and overwhelming to include form abilities on top of it. And aside for the thematic and mechanical reasons I have previously given, that sense of overwhelming odds is something I aggressively try to convey- angels ( hunter angels especially) are far, far greater than their demon counterparts in terms of their design and abilities- unless the entire group was to seriously tackle one, they will never ever be able to kill any of my higher ranked angels without use of it's Bane.. Now while I do have rank 1 angels who are admittedly weaker than my players.. they've never met any, even though they ironically are the most important pieces of the Machine's infrastructure in the area. Unlike many of my other games I've run where my players have often become quite powerful and almost unstoppable, I run Demon in a very F.E.A.R.( the original game) esque manner concerning the impact of any individual player: Major victories are not earned easily, and small victories are always fleeting.. though not without worth. Players need some bright spots after all XD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:02:12-07:00","id":856756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856736#post856736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, when you take Numina, Manifestations, and Incepts into account, it is very mean and overwhelming to include form abilities on top of it. And aside for the thematic and mechanical reasons I have previously given, that sense of overwhelming odds is something I aggressively try to convey- angels ( hunter angels especially) are far, far greater than their demon counterparts in terms of their design and abilities- unless the entire group was to seriously tackle one, they will never ever be able to kill any of my higher ranked angels without use of it's Bane..</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, using the Ephemeral Being rules as-written, I struggle to see a way a party could easily tackle a Rank 4-5 Angel even using its Bane so long as it has the right Influences. A Rank 5 Angel with, to take a totally random example, Time 5 as an Influence is about as untouchable as you can get. And that's without any additional powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856736#post856736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now while I do have rank 1 angels who are admittedly weaker than my players.. they've never met any, even though they ironically are the most important pieces of the Machine's infrastructure in the area. Unlike many of my other games I've run where my players have often become quite powerful and almost unstoppable, I run Demon in a very F.E.A.R.( the original game) esque manner concerning the impact of any individual player: Major victories are not earned easily, and small victories are always fleeting.. though not without worth. Players need some bright spots after all XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. I'm just saying that without Form Powers Angels already achieve that. With Form Powers I can't help but feel Angels would take the setting from dark and dangerous into the realms of overwhelming. I want my players scared and paranoid, not hopeless to the point of inaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:22:09-07:00","id":856760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856756#post856756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, using the Ephemeral Being rules as-written, I struggle to see a way a party could easily tackle a Rank 4-5 Angel even using its Bane so long as it has the right Influences. A Rank 5 Angel with, to take a totally random example, Time 5 as an Influence is about as untouchable as you can get. And that's without any additional powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree completely. I'm just saying that without Form Powers Angels already achieve that. With Form Powers I can't help but feel Angels would take the setting from dark and dangerous into the realms of overwhelming. I want my players scared and paranoid, not hopeless to the point of inaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I respect that greatly, it is a perfectly valid and logical point of note. And as much as I hate it, Dark Eras shows form abilities being used as numina. Doesn't change my stance mind, going to keep doing what I'm doing and treating form abilities as separate from numina,.. but I still accept that it's a perfectly fine way to do things -3- .<br /> <br /> It's odd, but that is the opposite reaction of my players actually. They see lots of opportunity for stealth and subterfuge. They know their enemies are incredibly powerful, so they do what the angels are only adequate at instead of possessing hyper capability: they go to ground and use guerilla warfare tactics and target what the angels are responsible for, not the angels themselves. My angels are typically more intelligent and adaptable than canon example angels, but they still have that robotic mentality towards concepts like improve and such. So it balances out incredibly well, surprisingly XD. And to go back to my F.E.A.R. analogy, at some points there have been feelings of hopelessness when things have gotten really bad, but the group still soldiered on. Their enemies won't stop hunting them, so they can't stop their efforts to foil the Machines plans.<br /> <br /> But, my players are not your players, so I understand completely. Like I said, I am aware of the unfairness of it.. so I am always making sure there are options out there so my players have some method of making it through the day. Adversity is something our group responds really well to haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:01:54-07:00","id":856779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856760#post856760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I respect that greatly, it is a perfectly valid and logical point of note. And as much as I hate it, Dark Eras shows form abilities being used as numina. Doesn't change my stance mind, going to keep doing what I'm doing and treating form abilities as separate from numina,.. but I still accept that it's a perfectly fine way to do things -3- .<br /> <br /> It's odd, but that is the opposite reaction of my players actually. They see lots of opportunity for stealth and subterfuge. They know their enemies are incredibly powerful, so they do what the angels are only adequate at instead of possessing hyper capability: they go to ground and use guerilla warfare tactics and target what the angels are responsible for, not the angels themselves. My angels are typically more intelligent and adaptable than canon example angels, but they still have that robotic mentality towards concepts like improve and such. So it balances out incredibly well, surprisingly XD. And to go back to my F.E.A.R. analogy, at some points there have been feelings of hopelessness when things have gotten really bad, but the group still soldiered on. Their enemies won't stop hunting them, so they can't stop their efforts to foil the Machines plans.<br /> <br /> But, my players are not your players, so I understand completely. Like I said, I am aware of the unfairness of it.. so I am always making sure there are options out there so my players have some method of making it through the day. Adversity is something our group responds really well to haha.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to say is that I'm getting that exact response from my players as-is, without giving angels any buffs beyond how they're written. Our last session ended with a big, climatic fight against an Angel in a burning building, but no one so much as took a swing against the Angel itself. They focussed on destroying the Infrastructure, using Interlocks, Form Powers, and Exploits to stop the Angel from using its powers against them directly, and ran like hell once Aether started to run dry. Actually winning the fight was never an option, so they just kept their focus on surviving long enough to complete their objective and get away. I guess my primary concern is that piling even more powers onto an already unstoppable character is unlikely to improve the mood in which players approach a fight with an angel with an attitude of having already lost.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it would mean another entry on the Angel's character sheet that needs to get filled out, and I like to keep my NPCs simple. I like that I can have a fully fleshed Angel done in a quarter of the time it takes to do the same to a Demon NPC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:21:00-07:00","id":856790,"title":"","content":"Wait, Angels use Form Abilities as Numina? On a semi-related note that may seem out of place here, does Going Loud allow you to use additional Form powers on a temporary basis? Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:39:09-07:00","id":856797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856779#post856779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm trying to say is that I'm getting that exact response from my players as-is, without giving angels any buffs beyond how they're written. Our last session ended with a big, climatic fight against an Angel in a burning building, but no one so much as took a swing against the Angel itself. They focussed on destroying the Infrastructure, using Interlocks, Form Powers, and Exploits to stop the Angel from using its powers against them directly, and ran like hell once Aether started to run dry. Actually winning the fight was never an option, so they just kept their focus on surviving long enough to complete their objective and get away. I guess my primary concern is that piling even more powers onto an already unstoppable character is unlikely to improve the mood in which players approach a fight with an angel with an attitude of having already lost.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it would mean another entry on the Angel's character sheet that needs to get filled out, and I like to keep my NPCs simple. I like that I can have a fully fleshed Angel done in a quarter of the time it takes to do the same to a Demon NPC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that is great!<br /> <br /> And huh.. Never had that problem with my players to be honest. They love challenges, the more deadly or dangerous the better lol.<br /> <br /> Im the opposite, I love taking a good ammountm of time building NPCs.. They are usually even more fleshed out than the player characters lmao","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:12:18-07:00","id":856812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856790#post856790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, Angels use Form Abilities as Numina? On a semi-related note that may seem out of place here, does Going Loud allow you to use additional Form powers on a temporary basis? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The angel Captor does, he has both Mirror Skin and Tether<br /> <br /> And unclear. Its possible, though I think that no, those extra form abilities do not manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:17:50-07:00","id":856817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856790#post856790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, Angels use Form Abilities as Numina? On a semi-related note that may seem out of place here, does Going Loud allow you to use additional Form powers on a temporary basis? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Going Loud provides access to all Exploits plus any Embeds related to your character's Archetype (unless you're playing an Analyst, in which case weird things happen).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856797#post856797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that is great!<br /> <br /> And huh.. Never had that problem with my players to be honest. They love challenges, the more deadly or dangerous the better lol.<br /> <br /> Im the opposite, I love taking a good ammountm of time building NPCs.. They are usually even more fleshed out than the player characters lmao</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick in any RPG, but particularly a horror game, is taking care to not totally disempower the players. Just, you know, mostly do it. As a GM it's pretty easy for me to make it so that the players cannot ever achieve anything they set out to do. Doing so would make for an awful game though. The problem is when the players, rightly or wrongly, get the impression that there is no chance of success. At that point they might step out of the game, break character, or worst of all stay silent as the frustration builds and they stop having fun. So yeah, play to your players by all means. I'd hardly say my players dislike a challenge, but a few of them are kind of rules-orientated characters who like to test systems and try to break the game. When a glance at the Ephemeral Being rules suggest that they will never be able to match even a mid-range Angel in a fight, I have to work through the story to give them a reason to stay invested. I don't really want to push them further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:25:22-07:00","id":856822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856817#post856817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Going Loud provides access to all Exploits plus any Embeds related to your character's Archetype (unless you're playing an Analyst, in which case weird things happen).<br /> The trick in any RPG, but particularly a horror game, is taking care to not totally disempower the players. Just, you know, mostly do it. As a GM it's pretty easy for me to make it so that the players cannot ever achieve anything they set out to do. Doing so would make for an awful game though. The problem is when the players, rightly or wrongly, get the impression that there is no chance of success. At that point they might step out of the game, break character, or worst of all stay silent as the frustration builds and they stop having fun. So yeah, play to your players by all means. I'd hardly say my players dislike a challenge, but a few of them are kind of rules-orientated characters who like to test systems and try to break the game. When a glance at the Ephemeral Being rules suggest that they will never be able to match even a mid-range Angel in a fight, I have to work through the story to give them a reason to stay invested. I don't really want to push them further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Am aware, it just typically isnt a problem XD. And I do my best to not depower the players, their enemies are just so much stronger lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:45:28-07:00","id":856830,"title":"","content":"You know, I don't think there's a game in the whole of World of Darkness where the player characters are as profoundly unequipped to fight their primary antagonists as Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:21:26-07:00","id":856930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856830#post856830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I don't think there's a game in the whole of World of Darkness where the player characters are as profoundly unequipped to fight their primary antagonists as Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you. I think thats part of the fun though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:29:22-07:00","id":856933,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, absolutely. It's vital for the game's mood, I think. Just an observation, not a criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:38:08-07:00","id":856939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856933#post856933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, absolutely. It's vital for the game's mood, I think. Just an observation, not a criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely need your list of angels at some point then lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:40:22-07:00","id":856940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856939#post856939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely need your list of angels at some point then lol</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the NPCs I've written for my game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:42:18