milieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:47:12-07:00","id":856944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856943#post856943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a whole Actual Play with them floating around here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that isn't them mechanically, I think lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:48:27-07:00","id":856945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856944#post856944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that isn't them mechanically, I think lol</div> </div> </div> </div>So picky <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll shoot you some PMs after work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:08:20-07:00","id":856953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=856945#post856945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So picky <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll shoot you some PMs after work.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a storyteller, picky is in the job description lol.<br /> <br /> good, and I look forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T10:52:09-07:00","id":857191,"title":"","content":"I have an idea. You could treat melee weapons, guns, armor, Cover and at least one method of keeping in touch with the G-M as inherent advantages of the Angel template. You no longer have to spend slots on Blast or Mortal Mask (but you would still need the Materialize Manifestation to interact directly with the material world). The freed up Numina slots can be spent on more specialized powers. <br /> <br /> In addition, Angelic Influences can mimic Demonic Forms, with the dots corresponding to the sophistication in most cases. That is, 1 dot = Modification, 2 dots = Technology, 3 dots = Propulsion, 4 dots = Process and 5 dots = epic advantages that go beyond Processes. You may use an Incept that allows Angels to have Influences rated higher than their Rank.<br /> <br /> For example: an Angel with Influence (Sound 4) might have Sonic Acuity and Voice Of The Angel. You wouldn't need to spend a slot on a sonic Rivet Arm, as your template gives you a gun for free.<br /> <br /> For 1 Essence, 2 &quot;Angelic Form&quot; advantages may be manifested reflexively. Assuming full &quot;Angelic Form&quot; costs nothing, but does not restore Essence and it triggers Aetheric Resonance.<br /> <br /> As for the rating of the free weapons and armor, I suggest using their Rank and function as guidelines. A Destroyer sent after a tough as nails Demon might have a plasma sword that deals its Rank + 1 as a Damage Bonus and bypasses any protection that isn't supernatural in some way. The simple switchblades that come out of the wrists of maintenance Angels should deal +1L at most. You may come up with an Incept to improve all these ratings for a scene if deemed necessary.<br /> <br /> That should be more than enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-01-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:01:27-07:00","id":857196,"title":"","content":"Sorry, double post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:40:22-07:00","id":857215,"title":"","content":"That is a very interesting concept, which deserves more exploring methinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:40:32-07:00","id":857443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857215#post857215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a very interesting concept, which deserves more exploring methinks.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the best way to do that is to come up with quick Angel concepts and play test them a little. Have a sniper Destroyer. I used some house rules to calculate the derived traits and made Innocuous give 9 Again to Stealth instead of +2. I'll leave the Ban &amp; Bane up to you.<br /> <br /> Virtue: Subtle<br /> Vice: Ruthless<br /> <br /> Rank: 3<br /> Attributes: Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Maximum Essence/Per Turn: 30/9<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 11<br /> Armor: 3/3<br /> <br /> Influences: Stealth 3, Sight 2<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Image, Materialize<br /> Numina: Hallucination, Innocuous, Pathfinder, Speed<br /> Angelic Form: Advanced Optics, Night Vision, Urban Fluidity, Spatial Distortion<br /> Incepts: Space<br /> <br /> Main Dice Pools:<br /> Searching 11 (May benefit from Advanced Optics and Night Vision)<br /> Stealth 11 With 9 Again (For walking; use Urban Fluidity, Spatial Distortion and the Speed Numen otherwise)<br /> <br /> Weapons/Attacks:<br /> Concealed Shiv [9 dice, +1L]<br /> Sniper Rifle [14 dice, +4L, Range 200/400/800, Thermal Scope]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-02-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:13:17-07:00","id":857466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857443#post857443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the best way to do that is to come up with quick Angel concepts and play test them a little. Have a sniper Destroyer. I used some house rules to calculate the derived traits and made Innocuous give 9 Again to Stealth instead of +2. I'll leave the Ban &amp; Bane up to you.<br /> <br /> Rank: 3<br /> Attributes: Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Maximum Essence/Per Turn: 30/9<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 11<br /> Armor: 3/3<br /> Influences: Stealth 3, Sight 2<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Image, Materialize<br /> Numina: Hallucination, Innocuous, Pathfinder, Speed<br /> Angelic Form: Advanced Optics, Night Vision, Urban Fluidity, Spatial Distortion<br /> Incepts: Space<br /> <br /> Main Dice Pools:<br /> Searching 11 (May benefit from Advanced Optics and Night Vision)<br /> Stealth 11 With 9 Again (For walking; use Urban Fluidity, Spatial Distortion and the Speed Numen otherwise)<br /> <br /> Weapons/Attacks:<br /> Concealed Shiv [9 dice, +1L]<br /> Sniper Rifle [14 dice, +4L, Range 200/400/800, Thermal Scope]</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that, though he should posses two more Incepts. Still, that is a pretty damn good example of a n angel with integrated weaponry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:29:13-07:00","id":857473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857466#post857466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that, though he should posses two more Incepts. Still, that is a pretty damn good example of a n angel with integrated weaponry</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, but isn't this deadly enough? Incepts are <i><b>terrifying</b>. </i>And ephemeral beings can spend Essence to increase their Attributes for a whole scene on a 1:1 ratio, up to a bonus of [Rank + 2]. Let's not forget that Angels can also be helped by Cultists, Cryptids and more. By the way, I added a Virtue and Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-02-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:09:43-07:00","id":857501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857473#post857473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks, but isn't this deadly enough? Incepts are <i><b>terrifying</b>. </i>And ephemeral beings can spend Essence to increase their Attributes for a whole scene on a 1:1 ratio, up to a bonus of [Rank + 2]. Let's not forget that Angels can also be helped by Cultists, Cryptids and more. By the way, I added a Virtue and Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, but angels possess a number of Incepts equal to Rank is all lol<br /> <br /> And angels by default do possess virtue and vice, though they are more robotic lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:19:25-07:00","id":857530,"title":"","content":"Tomorrow, or Rather later today I will post more of these angelic form abilities for you, As promised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:31:39-07:00","id":857537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857501#post857501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes, but angels possess a number of Incepts equal to Rank is all lol<br /> <br /> And angels by default do possess virtue and vice, though they are more robotic lol</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't have to fill every antagonist to the brim with powers and advantages. In fact, doing so would be unfair to your players. A sniper doesn't need an Incepted +30L laser cannon, that goes against the concept. Acrozatarim made a good point about this in the Claimed Power Guidelines thread. <br /> <br /> I think the Bans of Angels should be more severe than average, to balance Incepts and such. The sniper I posted might be forbidden from firing at anyone openly displaying a necklace with a complex design AND from firing into a common type of structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:39:01-07:00","id":857582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857537#post857537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't have to fill every antagonist to the brim with powers and advantages. In fact, doing so would be unfair to your players. A sniper doesn't need an Incepted +30L laser cannon, that goes against the concept. Acrozatarim made a good point about this in the Claimed Power Guidelines thread. <br /> <br /> I think the Bans of Angels should be more severe than average, to balance Incepts and such. The sniper I posted might be forbidden from firing at anyone openly displaying a necklace with a complex design AND from firing into a common type of structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if my players were any different, you would be absolutely right. However, I make my angels as formidable as I do for two reasons: the first being that I firmly believe that angels are meant to be unfair to an extent, its part of what makes Demon, well, demon. Outgunned and outmatched on all sides.<br /> <br /> The second is more simple: my players love challenges, sometime to the extreme. They get bored without serious opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:58:14-07:00","id":857627,"title":"","content":"Remember an Angel will not use its Incepts unless it needs/wants to alert every other Angel and Demon for miles around. And get authorization from the God Machine that such power is ok to use.<br /> <br /> Sniper Angel is scary, but quiet. It has no permission or need to use Incepts. Should the enemy become... more dangerous, urgent to put down, or whatever, it can thn seek permission and become more than a mere 'sniper' but possibly the very embodiment of 'Death from afar'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:40:12-07:00","id":857930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857627#post857627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember an Angel will not use its Incepts unless it needs/wants to alert every other Angel and Demon for miles around. And get authorization from the God Machine that such power is ok to use.<br /> <br /> Sniper Angel is scary, but quiet. It has no permission or need to use Incepts. Should the enemy become... more dangerous, urgent to put down, or whatever, it can thn seek permission and become more than a mere 'sniper' but possibly the very embodiment of 'Death from afar'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well unless the mission is in danger of failing.. Then permission seems to be freely given, since angels will use their Incepts without hesitation.<br /> <br /> And the sniper angel is pretty good, I freely admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:33:24-07:00","id":857999,"title":"","content":"And now, here are more angelic form abilities.. after half a day of web troubles XD<br /> <br /> Note, the scaling of utility and power does vary wildly a bit, though I did do my best to make them not too crazy. Constructive feedback is greatly appreciated ! Also, some abilities are noted to be incompatible with the Fall and thus are unavailable for demons to possess, and others are noted on how they change to fit the demonic form. Otherwise, they function much the same way for demons as well as angels.<br /> __________<br /> Imperial Raiment ( Angelic Modification)<br /> There are times where the Word must be heard by mortals, and in order to impress it upon those who are to receive it, sometimes Messengers are augmented with an appearance that matches the authority they represent, as well as offering a small amount of physical protection from attack.<br /> <br /> Appearance: The angel's form is gilded and encrusted with various gemstones, all which glow as if illuminated from within with thousands of tiny stars. A crown of phantasmal fire adorns the angel's head and a beautiful mosaic of images and iconography adorn it's body- all designed to awe and induce reverence for the angel and it's purpose.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: This Modification enhances the natural gravitas of it's bearer, subverting the minds and softening the hearts of those mortals who gaze upon it. Mortal characters who engage in social interactions with the angel suffer a penalty to resist it's maneuvers equal to half the angel's Finesse score rounded down. Supernatural targets find the penalty slightly lessened, being only equal to the angel's Rank. Imperial Raiment also offers greater defenses against attack, adding a + 1 to it's armor rating without inciting an Initiative penalty.<br /> <br /> Influence Enhancer ( Angelic Technology)<br /> Angels are called to perform a great many tasks over the course of their existence in the Service in the Machine, and the very Influences that every angel possess are among their greatest instruments. As such, those angels whose Missions revolve around manipulating anything from physical objects to living creatures to emotions and concepts are granted hardware needed to give these powers an extra boost.<br /> <br /> Appearance: This ability does not normally manifest as a physical aspect on the angel's form, being present more as indelible aura that alerts those capable of perceiving it that the angel is graced with an air of increased proficiency, along with an unshakable feeling of absolute purpose surrounding the angel.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: by spending a point of Essence to activate it; Influence Enhancer allows the angel who possesses this Technology to utilize their Influences as if they were one dot higher than their current level to a maximum of 5, for the remainder of the scene. This Technology has the added benefit of adding a + 2 to all rolls involving the angel's Influences. Should the user of this Technology Fall, they also lose access to this ability, instead being replaced with a very similar Technology called Exploit Enhancer.<br /> <br /> Aspect Shears ( Angelic Modification/Technology)<br /> A hundred thousand Projects require living sacrifices-human or otherwise-to function, and the vast majority of Psychopomps ( and occasionally Destroyers) are responsible for providing these sacrificial subjects. Some sacrifices are more particular, however, requiring incredibly specific materials and ingredients: The right hand of a thief who broke into a hundred homes before being caught or the heart of a truly righteous mother for example. For these sacrifices, angels are sometimes equipped with the means of shearing these pieces away from their victims- with said pieces miraculously remaining alive and unspoiled until they are ready for their purpose.<br /> <br /> Appearance: One of the angel's hands is replaced with a highly articulate pair of blades that greatly resemble scissors or garden shears, though the blades themselves are unnaturally long and sharp- easily being a foot or more in length, These shears are often engraved with arcane runes that no mortal ( or demon) can decipher, and typically glow slightly with a wan ruddy or yellow light in dark places.<br /> <br /> Function: These shears are meant for one thing- dismembering living beings without killing either the victim or the pieces the angel intends to cut away. The angel pays a point of essence and rolls for a standard melee attack with it's Power+ Finesse -The victims Defense + Stamina ( armor bonuses apply where applicable). On a successful attack instead of dealing damage, the shears instead painlessly cut away the desired limb or body part away, inflicting appropriate tilts such as Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Blind, and so on. There are exceptions, decapitation or removing the heart may leave the head or heart themselves alive, but the rest of the body dies without these vital pieces. Interestingly, and perhaps horrifyingly, this Modification can affect demonic form abilities just as easily as it can the flesh of more mundane creatures- stripping these powers away from the owners while leaving the abilities fully intact and operational in their shorn state. Like with mortals, demons are affected by the adverse tilts from losing limbs ( and potentially death), but also lose access to the corresponding abilities.<br /> <br /> However hope is not lost for the victims of these Shears, as long as these body parts are recovered before they are sacrificed, they can be put back in place with very little effort- the rightful owner's bodies accept these parts back as if they were never cut away in the first place, reattaching with no additional aid. Only an extended Dexterity + Medicine roll is required, with three successes needed to successfully restore the severed parts. As before, Unfortunately, once removed a head or heart cannot be replaced- their bodies are sadly dead and useless. It is possible that through Exploits or other magic the victim can be restored, albeit the particulars of such a feat are at the Storyteller's discretion.<br /> <br /> Note: This ability can survive the transition of an Angels Fall, where the Modification/Technology functions much the same, though the demon in question can graft stolen limbs to his own body or demonic form, gaining the traits or powers associated with whatever parts are integrated into the enterprising Unchained- though unfortunately the demon cannot strip away angelic powers with this ability, it has lost the potency to do so. ( Also I as unsure on what to classify it. It's a bit too strong to be either a Modification or Technology, but at the same time I don't see it as a Process.. also for those who are eagle eyed, this ability is inspired by the Collector from the Dark Eras book)<br /> <br /> Optimized Impulse Drives ( Angelic Propulsion)<br /> While many angels possess numina designed for rapid translocation, the Machine realizes that sometimes it is more advantageous to install it's agents with hardware to allow for rapid movement that does not require large expenditures of occult energy. Thus some angels possess internal and external machinery to allow for immense acceleration while remaining almost undetectable to enemies capable of sensing essence emissions.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Additional pistons and gears are built into the Angel's limbs, glowing with slight luminescence from within.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: with an expenditure of willpower, the angel activates its impulse drives, rolling Finesse + Rank and adding the successes to it's speed trait. These drives carry the added benefit of adding this speed modifier to activation rolls for numina that allow for supernatural speed or transportation- the extra hardware providing a boost to it's internal systems for the transit. Strangely, this propulsion does not function should the angel in question utilize Incepts such as Delivery or Motion- It must either choose to utilize this ability or the Incepts. Attempting to utilize both to augment each other overtaxes the angels' systems, dealing a number of points of lethal damage equal to the angel's Finesse as it experiences a destructive energy surge through it's internal structure.<br /> <br /> Note: This ability can be retained through the Fall, though naturally it does not interact with Numina or Incepts. As such, it is capable of being used to boost Exploits and Embeds with little difficulty- the strain on the demon is much lessened.<br /> <br /> Celestial Halo ( Angelic Process)<br /> The God-Machine, despite not being omniscient, is near omnipotent in it's mastery of universal forces. Being Its servants, it is only natural a number of them are bequeathed with a greater fraction of this dominance from time to time. Demons who know of this Process are often stricken with fear when they encounter an angelic sibling who possesses it; for they know these slaves have been granted freedom to make use of their greatest of powers for the advancement of their Missions- powers that blessed with a larger portion of their God's awesome might behind them.<br /> <br /> Appearance: A great, fiery halo of divine energy encircles or rests behind the angel's head. It's appearance varies widely from a simple lambent band of light to a intricately engraved blue-white gear made of lightning to a wheel of Dharma composed of golden flames, to anything in between.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: The Celestial Halo grants incredible power to those angels outfitted with it- and represent a grave danger to those who would interfere with their Missions. This Process doubles the efficiency of an angels' Incepts primary effects: Units' effect increases to twice the user's Rank + 2 for example. This Process also is embedded with programming imperatives that grant the user more operational freedom concerning its Incepts and their use, enabling the angel to utilize these root-codes with freedom a number of times equal to it's Rank+ 1 without violating it's Mission parameters- as long as the use of said Incepts do not directly endanger the Mission or cause it's failure ( i.e. destroying what the angel was assigned to protect, killing an excess number of mortals, etc). Naturally, should an angel who possesses this Process somehow Fall, this ability is lost along with its Incept privileges.<br /> <br /> Familiar-Drone ( Angelic Process)<br /> Some angels require additional eyes and hands to aid them with their Missions, and rather than assign multiple angels to a single assignment, the God-Machine instead equips it's servant with a semi-autonomous sub-unit that is capable of performing less strenuous or otherwise lower priority tasks while the angel tackles more pressing matters- though the drone does require support and upkeep from it's angelic \u201cplatform\u201d.<br /> <br /> Appearance: The bio-mechanical drone linked to the angel can possess a wide variety of forms: a iron feathered raven, an iridescent dragonfly with airfoils made of fiberglass and aluminum, or something as artificial as a rotor drone. The only things these familiars have in common are that they all possess the ability to fly, and all are anchored to/generated from some sort of docking structure built into the angel's body when not in use.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: The familiar drone uses the same ephemeral rules as angels, though with some alterations. These drones are treated as Rank 1 angels and possess four dots in each of their attributes; though their angel platform may choose to allocate dot's from their own Attributes to the drone, to a maximum of three dots per attribute in order to increase the servitors capabilities. In addition, a familiar-drone possesses three numina at it's disposal; two of it's user's choosing along with the Innocuous numen, as well as possessing a single dot in any Influence it's user chooses for it to have-provided the angel also has access to those Influences. Being ephemeral constructs like angels, the drone must make use of Manifestation conditions in order to effectively interact with the world around them, thus they are equipped with the Twilight Form and Materialization Manifestations. Due to their relative weakness and not being true angels, the drone cannot possess or utilize Incepts, though they can benefit from the effects of them should their platform deign to use one to empower them.<br /> <br /> These drones are size 1 and possess an Essence pool of 10 when fully fueled, and burn through 1 point of essence per day of being separated from their controller, though they might burn through their stores faster if pressed to defend themselves or utilize numina that require essence expenditure. Despite being semi-autonomous and possessing a surprising level of creativity when interpreting tasks given to them, the drones are virtually mindless when not performing functions assigned to them by their platform, and thus do not have willpower pools of their own, though like with Attribute allocation, the angel may imbue it's drone with it's own willpower points, up to a maximum of three. As the drones share a constant link to their controller, the angel is aware of it's drone at all times, and is able to send commands to the drone reflexively at no cost, or take direct control of the drone at any time with an expenditure of a willpower.<br /> <br /> An angel may only have one familiar-drone active at a time, though if the pre existing drone is destroyed, the angel may generate a new one at the cost of five essence. Attribute allocation, willpower investment, and essence transference can only be performed while the drone is docked with the angel, and is conducted on a 1:1 ratio per turn- the drone's systems are simply not advanced enough to handle power transfers of greater intensity.<br /> <br /> Note: Like others, this ability can be retained through the Fall, though the drone becomes a fully material construct and loses it's rank ( which is replaced by Primium), manifestations, utilizes embeds instead of numina, and is sustained through Aether. Otherwise the ability is unchanged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-02-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:37:21-07:00","id":858003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857930#post857930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well unless the mission is in danger of failing.. Then permission seems to be freely given, since angels will use their Incepts without hesitation..</div> </div> </div> </div>Less 'permission is freely given' and more 'Angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience'.<br /> <br /> Pride goeth before the Fall, after all. <br /> <br /> (As a story hook, remember that if your demons survive the encounter, they may be helping that ex-Angel out of a crater the next morning and welcoming him to life as an Unchained.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:52:42-07:00","id":858010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858003#post858003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less 'permission is freely given' and more 'Angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience'.<br /> <br /> Pride goeth before the Fall, after all.<br /> <br /> (As a story hook, remember that if your demons survive the encounter, they may be helping that ex-Angel out of a crater the next morning and welcoming him to life as an Unchained.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Halo is the God Machine essentially stating, &quot;If I am adding this, the angel will NEED to use these powers I don't really like.&quot; as a result, it is incredibly rare, but illustrates sometimes subtly is not an option and the full might of God needs to be called upon.Cause remember, angels will readily use Incepts if the Mission is in danger anyway, so more &quot;angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience&quot; is a bit redundant to me. But I will tweak it a bit, making it's use less forgiving.<br /> <br /> and that is a pretty good story hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:42:15-07:00","id":858031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858010#post858010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause remember, angels will readily use Incepts if the Mission is in danger anyway, so more &quot;angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience&quot; is a bit redundant to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Readily use if the mission is in danger' is different from 'if the angel's mission is compromised, this reluctance disappears, replaced by vengeance and an angel prepared to use its full power'. If the angel uses Incepts while on-mission without authorisation, it will effectively compromise and fail its mission anyway.<br /> <br /> If the mission is already failed (a 'compromised' mission by definition will not succeed the way the God-Machine intends. Even if the outcome appears the same, it's not what the God-Machine wanted), a vengeful angel may allow emotion to take hold, and will likely compromise itself further, and will either be recycled for a better unit, or may Fall.<br /> <br /> 'Angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience' isn't redundant. The angel is specifically <i>gambling</i> on the God-Machine being satisfied enough with the results that it doesn't punish or scrap the angel. When acting on emotion this way, the odds usually aren't in the angel's favour.<br /> <br /> I think Halo is an overreach anyway. If the angel is authorised with freedom to choose to use Incepts a certain number of times in a mission, that's enough without expanding the Incept effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858010#post858010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that is a pretty good story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:10:12-07:00","id":858052,"title":"","content":"I like those Angelic Form advantages, Korogra. I just don't know if Demons really need Aspect Shears. If they want to use biological components of mortals and supernaturals as Gadget Hardware without killing them, you could add that function to the Living Installation Exploit, and replace the body part with a Gadget of the donor's choice as recompense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:18:57-07:00","id":858057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858052#post858052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like those Angelic Form advantages, Korogra. I just don't know if Demons really need Aspect Shears. If they want to use biological components of mortals and supernaturals as Gadget Hardware without killing them, you could add that function to the Living Installation Exploit, and replace the body part with a Gadget of the donor's choice as recompense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point, it is a very valid question. But at the same time it reminds me of a friend once asking why a demon would really need Rain of Fire when they have the Incendiary and Hellfire Exploits. And to answer that question, I would just say that it is an alternative to the Exploits haha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:26:14-07:00","id":858062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858031#post858031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Readily use if the mission is in danger' is different from 'if the angel's mission is compromised, this reluctance disappears, replaced by vengeance and an angel prepared to use its full power'. If the angel uses Incepts while on-mission without authorisation, it will effectively compromise and fail its mission anyway.<br /> <br /> If the mission is already failed (a 'compromised' mission by definition will not succeed the way the God-Machine intends. Even if the outcome appears the same, it's not what the God-Machine wanted), a vengeful angel may allow emotion to take hold, and will likely compromise itself further, and will either be recycled for a better unit, or may Fall.<br /> <br /> 'Angel considers mission failure worse than disobedience' isn't redundant. The angel is specifically <i>gambling</i> on the God-Machine being satisfied enough with the results that it doesn't punish or scrap the angel. When acting on emotion this way, the odds usually aren't in the angel's favour.<br /> <br /> I think Halo is an overreach anyway. If the angel is authorised with freedom to choose to use Incepts a certain number of times in a mission, that's enough without expanding the Incept effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I think this is a cause of differences in interpretation. I sort of see the fact that angels suddenly losing the hesitance of using their Incepts as them getting authorization really. Vengeance or not, that sort of confidence quite clearly says to me &quot;mission parameter update&quot;. now obviously this isn't going to be the case every single time; the God-Machine makes mistakes and so do it's angels... but I sort of like the idea of this apparently universal change in demeanor being a sort of indication to authorization.<br /> <br /> Oh well, I might fix it so it just gives the freedom without the increase of capability.<br /> <br /> And you're welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:17:50-07:00","id":858085,"title":"","content":"You're absolutely welcome to interpret it how you want, and I apologise that through rewriting, cutting to meet word count, and editing, the intent of the sentence has become cloudier. To be clear, the intent was that angels with compromised missions are often pissed off and no longer care that they don't have authorisation. It wasn't meant to imply that the God-Machine included a standard clause in its mission instructions that reads 'When you've screwed up, go loud, it's all good'. Notably, the <i>God-Machine</i> doesn't include that clause, because who knows how much additional damage to Its plans the angel can do by throwing caution and mission parameters to the wind.<br /> <br /> Wheels within wheels, or more apt, cogs within cogs. Breaking some part of the machine is regrettable but may be able to be salvaged. Reacting to the breakage by grabbing a hammer and smashing everything in sight almost always makes everything worse, even if it makes the smasher temporarily feel better.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:40:59-07:00","id":858095,"title":"","content":"While that makes sense.. It doesnt sound right for angels to uniformly do that. Again that may be due to spacing constraints, but that doesnt sound like something an Analyst or a Psychopomp or Messenger would just do. Exceptions always exist.. But for those Incarnations... I dont see it happening that often. With Destroyers or Guardians, its much more believeable. So if it is okay with you, I am going with my interpretatiin XD.<br /> <br /> On that note, sometimes smashing everything can fix everything... If you are making a clean slate that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . ten years of being on strike crews have taught me that much lmao","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:44:05-07:00","id":858096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858095#post858095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if it is okay with you, I am going with my interpretatiin XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your game, so doesn't matter if it's okay with me as long as you have fun. That said, it's absolutely okay with me for you to run with it however you want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:55:55-07:00","id":858098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858096#post858096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's your game, so doesn't matter if it's okay with me as long as you have fun. That said, it's absolutely okay with me for you to run with it however you want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:15:56-07:00","id":858102,"title":"","content":"And I should have a small handful more for everyone tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T08:47:00-07:00","id":858357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=853899#post853899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. One of my biggest struggles running DtD has been making angels more than just spirits that show up when player flubs a compromise roll. As is, angels have a very limited budget of Numina (3 per rank) and most of their dice pools are pretty limited until they hit rank three, or start spending essence to boost them, which can get expensive.<br /> <br /> There's something visceral about talking to a guy, thinking he's just a guy, then having his hand turn into a drill of liquid metal and starting to spit acid... that gets a player's attention in a way that a Numen or an Influence just doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One way I look at making angels for my game is first I think about what infrastructures are going to be, will be and are there. Then thinking of the goal of that infrastructure think of what will be need to run it, create it, destroy it or maintain it. That's when you start building angels for the occult matrxies in the area.<br /> <br /> Ex.<br /> <br /> infrastructure is a mom and pop video game store. The Goal of this infrastructure is to give games to people who have an odd genetic tick that makes them more susceptible to mental persuasions of the god machine.<br /> <br /> So what will this store need. (Angels or cults can be put into anyone of these steps. So you don't need an angel for each one.)<br /> <br /> 1. Someone to make the games. So this could be a messenger angel or a psychopomp angel.<br /> 2. Someone to build and run the store. This once again could be a psychopomp angel.<br /> 3. Protection of the store. This will be done by combination of Guardian angels and cultists<br /> 4. Collection of data on the stores output. This in my head could be done in a clever way by analyst angel. The game has always online DRM that is the angel.<br /> <br /> Once the targets are showen to be affected the god machine might move to make it so these targets now breed more to spreed there manipulated genes into the population as a whole or maybe the god machine ends this project with the elimination of these targets...these beta testers.<br /> <br /> So if it continues then more angels. cultists are added if not then a single destroyer angel with an elimination infrastructure could destroy the store.<br /> <br /> hmmmm just coming up with this I think I will now use this. Excuse me while I go to start building this into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":".  added a note 04-04-2016, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:59:43-07:00","id":858404,"title":"","content":"Three more for you guys!<br /> __<br /> <br /> Essence Tracer ( Angelic Technology)<br /> Hunting demons is not as difficult as one might think. The Unchained are a paranoid and suspicious lot by nature, especially concerning anything that may have connections to the God-Machine, and a hunter-angel with the right tools can exploit that curiosity with ease. This Technology allows the angel to discreetly inject a mortal with a species of Essence that degrades over time and releases pulses of Aether \u2013 turning said mortal into an occult red herring and fishing lure all at once.<br /> <br /> Appearance: One of the angel's hands become a medical injection tool with a repository that holds a small amount of liquefied Essence, which glows an ethereal blue-green.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: The angel is capable of summoning or dismissing the injector at will as an instant action. To utilize the injector, the angel makes a touch attack by rolling Power+Finesse \u2013 the subject's defense. On success the injector penetrates the skin but causes no damage, instead infusing a number of the angel's Essence points that the user elects to transfer to the mortal- up to the number the user can normally spend in a single turn. These Essence points are subtly altered by the injector upon infusion; normally Essence that is trapped within a human's body begins to fester, causing the human to sicken as if poisoned, but these points instead will dissipate at a rate of one point per hour until all injected points are gone. When these essence points do dissipate they release a small burst of Aether, which demons can detect and harvest as normal. As an added bonus, the injected Essence doubles as an etheric tracking device, allowing the angel in question to be aware of the mortal's exact location as long as she is within a radius of half the angel's Rank in miles ( minimum of one)- providing there is still Essence in her system. Seemingly normal humans that randomly release Aether are sure to attract the attentions of the Unchained that may be hiding in the area, and as a result the hunter-angel gains a +2 to rolls related to searching out and discovering hiding demons.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that such exposure to Aether over the protracted period of time may lead to the mortal in question to become Stigmatic, though the chances of this occurring vary with the amount of Essence infused into their system. At one or two points, the chances of becoming Stigmatic are very low, at three there is a good change the Aetheric pulses will impart a Stigmata on the unwitting dupe. At four to five, the subject will become Stigmatic. However, the storyteller does possess full discretion when deciding whether or not this transformation occurs or not, should they or should they not wish for this Technology to unintentionally create Stigmatic liabilities for the angel in questions' Mission.<br /> Note: This ability can be retained by demons, though it injects Aether instead of Essence, making it a great tool for providing distractions to occupy angelic pursuers and their agents.<br /> <br /> Phase-shift Quickswitch ( Angelic Modification)<br /> Being ephemeral beings angels can quickly, if not easily, phase between material and immaterial states of existence. With this Modification the angel can benefit from her immaterial nature for a brief instant while remaining a physical entity.<br /> <br /> Appearance: The angel's body seems to become insubstantial for brief jolts of time, allowing tiny particles of dust and floatsam to pass through it's form, though the transition is too quick to allow larger, more solid objects to pass through.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: This Modification allows the angel to benefit from it's Twilight Form Manifestation for brief instant without having to resort fully becoming invisible and immaterial. By spending a point of Essence to activate it, the angel partially phases into it's twilight state, then returns to material form an instant later. By doing so, the angel is able to reflexively avoid any single attack that affects purely physical objects and retain it's instant action during the same turn( example; using Phase-shift Quickswitch to avoid the melee attack of an opponent and then responding with a melee attack of one's own). This Modification can only be used once per turn against a single source of harm- it does not function against multiple attackers.<br /> <br /> Note: Being fully material entities, demons have a slightly altered version, allowing them to instead shift from physical form to Twilight Form as an instant action \u2013 though shifting back to material form costs a point of willpower on top of the Aether cost and inflicts a single point of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Burning Sword ( Angelic Modification)<br /> Destroyers are most often deployed to hunt down and annihilate rogue operatives and other occult undesirables that plague the God-Machine. To ensure operation success, the Machine routinely outfits it's warriors with the highest grade weaponry for the task. Angels armed with this form ability are fearsome demon killers, for their swords inflict grievous wounds upon the flesh of doomed Unchained.<br /> <br /> Appearance: One of the angel's hands is a great and terrible sword of fiery Essence, it's shape and intensity varying widely from angel to angel, the only thing they have in common is that for demons they bring almost certain death.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: Burning Sword shares weaponry traits with the demonic Blade Hand Modification, with two exceptions. The first being that the angel has the option of adding it's Rank to the weapon's damage modifier with an expenditure of two Essence, stoking the sword's flames to a greater intensity. The second being that when the angel makes a successful attack against a demonic opponent or a Cryptid with Aether in it's system, the flaming blade reacts to those Aether stores violently, inflicting aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Note: should the angel possessing this Modification Fall, the weapon is warped by the resulting energies and loses these characteristics, becoming the Blade Hand Modification.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually I lied.. here is one more haha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Increased Essence Storage ( Angelic Process)<br /> Essence is the life blood the God-Machine, and by extension angels- without it the former would be diminished and the latter would fall into hibernation forever. This does not deter the Machine from sending Its servants on long missions where the possibility to regain this vital resource is scarce. To compensate for this potential liability, the Machine builds these servants with additional storage systems in order to remain well fueled on their assignments.<br /> <br /> Appearance: The angel has some sort of external container of some kind on it's body. I could resemble anything from a back mounted propane tank to an array of solar panels to a layer of fat on a fleshy angel's body.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: Increased Essence Storage allows the angel to store an additional five points of Essence per dot of Rank, to a maximum of five.( ie, Exampiel 1.0 is a Rank 1 angel, so he holds an additional 5 Essence, while Exampiel 3.0 is Rank 3, so she is able of storing 15 extra points, and Exampiel 5.0 as a Rank 5 angel can store a frightening extra 25 Essence) These stores are housed separately from the angel's primary Essence pool, unusable until it transfers essence from extra storage system into her main \u201ctank\u201d as it were. Increased Essence Storage can be refueled as easily as the angel itself, though Essence is only added to the Process once the angel's main stores are full.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-03-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:38:16-07:00","id":858628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858357#post858357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what will this store need.<br /> <br /> 1. Someone to make the games. So this could be a messenger angel or a psychopomp angel.<br /> 2. Someone to build and run the store. This once again could be a psychopomp angel.<br /> 3. Protection of the store. This will be done by combination of Guardian angels and cultists<br /> 4. Collection of data on the stores output. This in my head could be done in a clever way by analyst angel. The game has always online DRM that is the angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of angels in such a condensed area 0_0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:50:48-07:00","id":858636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=858628#post858628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of angels in such a condensed area 0_0</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. You only need a Psychopomp to build the mind-affecting parts of the games, with the rest being handled by unwitting mortals and maybe an Analyst. The G-M would never create 4 Angels for a task that can be completed with two or one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T18:57:01-07:00","id":858672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b