 You had 1 or 2 angels that that built stuff and then leave which happens all the time with infrastructures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:14:14-07:00","id":859284,"title":"","content":"You could spread that out even more by having the Guardian patrol a number of sites/Infrastructure, of which the video store is but one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T22:37:44-07:00","id":859472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=859284#post859284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could spread that out even more by having the Guardian patrol a number of sites/Infrastructure, of which the video store is but one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a host of its own problems though... one guarding several sites is very risky","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-05-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T03:49:59-07:00","id":859541,"title":"","content":"Using or not using an Angel at all is risky. It's all about risk vs reward, and where the Machine's calculations land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T05:15:57-07:00","id":859559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=859541#post859541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using or not using an Angel at all is risky. It's all about risk vs reward, and where the Machine's calculations land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but assigning a single Guardian to protect several pieces of Infrastructure is a gamble that has too large an margin for error to be a acceptable solution, unless the Guardian in question was of high rank, had the ability to be in several places at once/possessed multiple bodies, had several cultists assisting it, or some combination of all these xD.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, not saying it doesn't happen... it just seems to be a glitch in the Machines' computing to assign only one defender to a slew of Projects is all. Which could be a hook in itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:55:42-07:00","id":859711,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Or it could be an attempt at misdirection - <i>which</i> of the locations the Guardian guards are important, and which are Decoys? Or is this all an elaborate trap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:23:59-07:00","id":859730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=859711#post859711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Or it could be an attempt at misdirection - <i>which</i> of the locations the Guardian guards are important, and which are Decoys? Or is this all an elaborate trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its' not a good trap though, least not one worth using angelic assets; a seasoned( smart) Ring in all likely hood would probably observe all, it's pretty easy to tell what Infrastructure is meant to dupe and which is actually important- despite what fiction tells us. Now that sort of logic could easily be taken advantage of by the Machine to make the trap work.. but in my head such tactics are too wasteful for the Machine to use with any real regularity. Then again my Machine is more lucid with it's resources and makes far fewer glitches- Nigh Omniscient and Nigh Omnipotent translates to very few mistakes to me. No Hispanic angels who don't speak Spanish here lol<br /> <br /> I do agree that such an attempt at misdirection would be a likely scenario, but that could easily be taken care of by cultists, the more zealous the better. A single Guardian who has to patrol ten dupe sites while protecting the actual prize is only as effective as the angel.. and really, one Guardian doing such a thing screams &quot; trap&quot; for better or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-05-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:27:04-07:00","id":860329,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Do you mind me referencing these/this thread in the Cannibalization Merit <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\">here</a>? It strikes me a thematic for certain Saboteurs to prey on Angels for their Form Abilities (if Angels have Form Abilities, that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:51:57-07:00","id":860606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=860329#post860329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Do you mind me referencing these/this thread in the Cannibalization Merit <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>? It strikes me a thematic for certain Saboteurs to prey on Angels for their Form Abilities (if Angels have Form Abilities, that is).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm perfectly fine with it bud, feel free to do so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:08:17-07:00","id":860930,"title":"","content":"Done. I added the caveat that Demons can only steal the &quot;Fallen&quot; version of them, as the Angelic ones are designed at a higher power level in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T06:31:38-07:00","id":861004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=860930#post860930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Done. I added the caveat that Demons can only steal the &quot;Fallen&quot; version of them, as the Angelic ones are designed at a higher power level in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Pretty nifty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:04:47-07:00","id":861088,"title":"","content":"Sadly I hit a bit of a stump with whole cloth Angelic Form abilities for the time being, so for now, I will give a few examples of pre existing form abilities modified for angelic use, this first one being very MIB esque <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Magnesium Flare ( Angelic Process)</b><br /> Sometimes the messages that the servants of the God-Machine deliver come in strange forms, conveyed through methods beyond merely auditory. Angels equipped with this process are capable of encoding light waves with secret messages meant only for those who behold it's radiant form. Angels also sometimes use this light to manipulate of mortals in order to operate unimpeded- while the hapless crowd is left dazed and none the wiser thanks to false memories being imparted to them by the mind bending light.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's body is lit from within by a soft, warm light that can quickly grow in intensity at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel can spend a point of Essence and make a Power+ Finesse roll against a target's Resolve + Composure. On success the angel emits a near blinding burst of light that pulsates at a frequency that is only distinct to the intended recipient. This target then receives the Inspired Condition, with a focus invariably towards some project of the God-Machine or another, the specifics being at the storyteller's discretion. It should be noted that this particular effect is tied to the angel's Mission at hand, thus can only affect those individuals the God-Machine has commanded the angel to affect. Alternatively, the light can also be used to non lethally cover up certain occult incidents and turn mortal attention from delicate Infrastructure. Instead of the Inspired Condition, the angel can impart the False Memories Condition to witnesses, the contents of said memories being provided by either the angel or the God-Machine itself. In groups of mortals, the angel rolls against the highest present Resolve+ Composure score ( the idea being that if the strongest willed human is affected, the others will be affected alongside them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-23-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T06:57:02-07:00","id":867539,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, sorry for such a long pause for these things; work, life problems and a light bout of depressive thoughts had killed my muse for a bit, but it is back and I designed another handful of Angelic Form abilities for you guys to look at if you wanted! Please note that a couple of these are a tiny bit confusing, but that is because I am woefully unfamiliar with heavy weapons in CoD and I was experimenting with how to play with Multiple Images without making it utterly unstoppable.<br /> _________<br /> <b>Medichanic Tools (Angelic Modification)</b><br /> Wheels are custodians of the God-Machine and keep It from falling into complete disrepair and ruin. Angels of all types are pieces of the great Machine as well, and it is often the duty of some Psychopomps to diagnose and repair their brethren who are damaged or malfunctioning. To accomplish this the Machine equips these angels with a suit of tools needed to effectively mend the torn ligaments and shattered metal hides of their fellows.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's hands appear to be either covered with or composed of a pale latex like material, and each finger on one hand possesses a different medical tool ( one being a scalpel blade, another a medical stapler, a third being a hypodermic needle, etc) while the other possesses several mechanic tools ( an arc welder, a drill, an industrial glue dispenser and the like) - each that can be effortlessly retracted when not in use.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel is capable of rapidly healing their fellow angels. By paying a point of Essence and performing an extended Finesse+ Rank roll the user is capable of repairing damaged angelic comrades at a rate a number of bashing damage levels equal to Rank or one lethal damage per every two successes until the angel stops or all damage is repaired. This Modification can be used to treat aggravated wounds to a fellow angel's corpus, though it requires a point of Essence per level of damage every five successes rolled.<br /> <br /> While this Modification's primary ability only works on angels, though some Unchained posit that angels with this ability can repair demons as well, these medical tools do provide a + 3 bonus to treating and stabilizing wounded mortal beings. This ability cannot be used to repair one's own damaged body.<br /> <br /> Note: This ability can be utilized by demons as well, the only changes being the Aether cost and the bonus to treating non demons being lowered to + 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Data Storage ( Angelic Technology)</b><br /> Some Angels are required to perform Missions where subtly and caution are less required, or alternatively are assigned Missions that are highly dangerous \u2013 in either case a greater selection of occult programming is required than an angel normally possess. For these situations the God-Machine installs the proper hardware needed to allow for such data, allowing the angel to make use of more Numina than what she is normally capable of.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's body plays host to some sort of external data storage- a back mounted hardrive, numerous ports along her arms and shoulders that sport USB devices like skintags, or something more esoteric like a collection of glowing crystals or reinforced glass casings that hold tiny brains along the angel's spine.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel has access to four additional Numina of either her or the God Machine's choice. In addition, the extra hardware lends a slight increase of proficiency with any numen she chooses to make use of, adding a + 2 to activation rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Caustic Armor Gel (Angelic Modification)</b><br /> Guardians are the bane of many demons; their skill in battle great and their defenses legendary. Some Shields are commissioned by the God-Machine to be more defense oriented or inconspicuous for their Missions and as such are not designed with many offensive options in favor for more formidable defensive systems. In this context Caustic Armor Gel is an effective compromise, existing as a fusion of light armor and reactive weapon system.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's entire body is coated in a layer of a thick, gel like substance that seems to shimmer with several hues of color much like a puddle of motor oil on a sunny day. In response to physical trauma the afflicted area of the gel layer violently bubbles and balloons out before abruptly bursting, likely coating the offending instigator in caustic liquid after which the gel regenerates<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: Caustic Armor Gel grants the angel an armor rating of 2/1 that is capable of stacking with existing armor bonuses while posing no initiative penalty. In addition should the angel be struck by a successful melee attack this semi-liquid armor reacts by bubbling out and splattering against the opponent, requiring a reflexive Dex+ Athletics roll with a - 3 penalty to avoid being covered in the viscous substance. This liquid is highly caustic towards flesh and many inorganic materials, inflicting 2 points of lethal damage during the initial chemical splatter as well as inflicting an additional point of lethal damage every turn it is in contact with the affected individual- only quickly washing the substance off and removing any clothing stained by the substance will spare the victim of additional damage. This reactive trait of the form ability only applies to melee attacks such as Brawl or Weaponry, ranged weapons or supernatural attacks that do damage at range do not trigger the effect.<br /> <br /> Note: This form ability can be retained by demons, and functions the same for them as it does for angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Worm-hole Generator (Angelic Propulsion)</b><br /> Time and space are playthings the God-Machine and by proxy angels as well. Sometimes mortal agents must be allowed to benefit from these privileges that angels make trivial use of, so the Machine equips it's children with advanced hardware capable of twisting gravity, space, and time in a limited fashion \u2013 creating worm holes that connect two or more points in space together, allowing mortal servants to quickly move through an environment as a group.. or tactically positioning themselves to flank and surround enemies of the Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: A large portion of the Angel's abdomen has been replaced with a well shielded device that houses a gravitational singularity. The device possesses a small blast door like covering that separates the singularity from the outside world, though it opens up when the angel has need of it- displaying the mind-bending vortex within.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel with this Propulsion is capable of locally manipulating the spacial fabric of the local area, enabling the angel to create portals anywhere in his line of sight with a expenditure of Essence and a Power + Finesse roll, and the angel is able to generate a number of portals equal to twice it's Rank ( allowing for the absolute minimum of two connecting points to be established.) These tunnels in time and space enable those who enter one to emerge from others instantly on the same turn, and allow a number of people equal to the angel's successes pass through them before closing- the angel included. Physical obstructions do not hinder the angel's ability to create these worm holes as long as he is able to see around them- a solid concrete wall will prevent the angel from summoning a portal in the room behind it, but not a security door with a bullet-proof glass window allowing him to see into the secured room offers no hindrance to this piece of occult technology. Exceptions to this are rooms or locations that are supernaturally warded or otherwise shielded against unwanted intrusion or translocation- the Process fails automatically in these instances, for such feats are beyond it's capabilities.<br /> <br /> There are other limitations to what the angel's Worm-hole Generator can accomplish however; This Propulsion can only open portals within an area that is within the angel's direct line of sight ( which admittedly can be quite far with the proper Modifications), and tools or powers that allow the angel to remotely view other locations \u2013 such as a CCTV camera monitor or a ability to observe people or places without being physically present do not allow the angel to generate portals in those areas. In addition this Propulsion cannot open gateways to other realities or timelines, although it is capable of functioning within alternate worlds such as the Shadow, Hedge, or Underworld or Splinter Timelines more or less. Within the Shadow Realm or Underworld or an alternate timeline the Propulsion functions normally, though in the Hedge or any other realm where time and space are more fluid the Worm-hole Generator is more spotty- inflicting a -2 penalty to rolls for using it.<br /> <br /> Note: this is one of the few abilities that survive the Fall nearly unchanged, it's Essence and Rank statistics being replaced with Aether and Primium.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Multiple Images (Angelic Process)</b><br /> Angels are luminous beings constructed from the God-Machine's Essence and incomprehensible biomechanical aptitude, and as such are not bound by the physical constraints of possessing a single form- at least those angels who possess this form ability. With Multiple Images an angel can create hard light replicas of itself in order to accomplish multiple tasks at once, or to use as decoys and cannon fodder against particularly troublesome adversaries.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel is covered in dozens of strange symbols, each representing the angel itself. On command these symbols will detach from the angel before transforming into a perfect replica of whatever form the angel is currently assuming.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: With an expenditure of two Essence and a point of Willpower the angel is able to create a number of copies of itself equal to twice its Rank +2. These copies are perfect physical replicas and are impossible to distinguish from the original through passing observation. This isn't to say that these replicas are perfect copies in every sense; for while they are physical entities that are perfectly capable of interacting with the material world they are mere shadows of the angel they resemble. The replicas share the angel's Power, Finesse, Resistance, Size, Willpower and defense traits, but are unable to spend Essence or make use of the angel's Influences, Manifestations, Numina, Incepts, or Form Abilities that require Essence ( though they can still make use of others, a sword-hand is still a sword and wings are still capable of flight for example)- in fact they cannot make use of form abilities at all if none were manifested at the time of their creation. It should be noted that this form ability can be activated a number of times equal to the angel's rank per scene, allowing the angel to quickly create a rather impressive crowd of copies ( though this number pales in comparison to the illusionary hordes the demonic version of this ability conjures up.) These replicas persist for either a scene or until the angel who created them dismisses them, at which point they dissolve into a softly glowing nimbus of color before fading away completely, the symbols that represented them reappearing on the angel's body.<br /> <br /> These copies also are quite fragile, possessing only a single level of Corpus. Should a replica sustain only a single point of bashing it is still capable of functioning, though it's form has begun to destabilize, the body sporadically shimmering as thick, shaky lines of static crisscross its form at regular intervals, it's moments now jerky as if malfunctioning slightly. Taking a point of lethal or aggravated damage destroys the replica, which explodes in a cloud of semi-solid light particles.<br /> <br /> Despite these weaknesses, these copies serve their purpose well and offer a nearly invaluable advantage to the angel- multiple eyes and hands with which to perform one's Mission more effectively. The angel is capable of communicating with these light-clones at any distance and can direct them with nothing but a thought, allowing for complex tactical maneuvers and seamless cooperation, granting a + 4 to all teamwork rolls performed by the angel and its copies. In combat the clones are perfectly able of acting independently, and while they lack the toughness or supernatural might of the original they are quite clever and dangerously resourceful in confrontations- using any advantage or weapon that is at hand in order to counteract threats to themselves or the original angel- factors that can easily prove to become deadly should a demon grow over confident due to the fragility and lack of flashy powers of these replicas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Swarm Missile Hive ( Angelic Process)</b><br /> Insects are dangerous creatures and are quite often used as part of a divine entity's arsenal of plagues to unleash upon mankind- several of the plagues inflicted upon Egypt involved insects and parasites, and great swarms of creatures resembling horrid locust like chimera will torment humans during the tribulations of mankind as described in the book of Revelation. The God-Machine is all to happy to make use of such creatures as well in order to punish it's adversaries, and some Destroyers possess hive-like structures built into their bodies that host teeming swarms of biomechanical wasp-like creatures which exist to be utilized as living warheads against enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's body possesses a bulbous biomechanical hive structure somewhere on it's body, usually on the back or abdomen to limit interference with the host's range of movement, along with various opening on various points of it's form - typically resembling either vents or fleshy orifices. Occasionally mechanical insects with fleshy abdomens of various colors can be seen entering and exiting the hive or it's myriad \u201ctunnels\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: This Process allows the angel to manufacture and house a number of varieties of biomechanical wasps that are meant to be utilized as living ammunition. The hive generates three default \u201cspecies\u201d of bio-warheads; Incendiary, Concussive, and Corrosive, though the angel in question is able to modify the Hive's on board programming in order to design new variations \u2013 the ingenuity to override this programming, even to aid in one's Mission, is often a subtle sign that the angel in question is on the path to Falling however. The hive can store up to eighty of these wasp-like creatures at a time and is able to manufacture replacement Swarm Missiles at a rate of five missiles per hour, although should the angel need ammunition immediately, she can expend a point of Essence to supercharge the hive's production capabilities \u2013 generating three missiles of the angel's choice per point of Essence spent.<br /> <br /> Incendiary Swarm Missiles possess a damage rating of 3L and upon detonation release a small amount of napalm like material that ignites and catches anything it touches on fire, with the intensity of a torch, the initial liquid burning out a number of turns equal to twice the angel's Rank. Five or more of these missiles used in a given area causes the Inferno Tilt in the area.<br /> <br /> Concussive Swarm Missiles are a non-lethal variation intended for crowd control. Concussive missiles have a damage rating of 2B and upon detonation unleash a burst of force that inflicts the Knocked Down Tilt on the target any any other creature within three yards should they fail a Dex+ Athletics roll with a -3 penalty.<br /> <br /> Corrosive Swarm Missiles are primarily intended for demolition/Infrastructure Elimination based objectives, though these missiles are just as effective in an anti-personnel or anti-armor role as well. These deadly missiles are 0A weapons and upon impact explode in a burst of an acidic gel-like fluid. This fluid is particularly active, and will continue to corrode covered targets for a number of turns equal to the angel's Rank before becoming inert- inflicting one point of aggravated damage per turn.<br /> <br /> The angel's hive grants her the ability to fire it's living missiles at opponents with a Power+ Finesse + Rank \u2013 target's defense+ Armor/Durability ( if applicable) \u2013 with the option of targeting a single opponent or object a number of times equal to half the angel's Rank rounded down or multiple targets equal to it's Rank in a single turn ( though the angel must still roll against each opponent/object separately.) The missiles possess a range of 50/100/300, making them relatively close to mid range weapons.<br /> <br /> As a final resort, angels can utilize a final \u201ccarpet bombing\u201d feature of the hive, simultaneously firing it's entire payload of missiles at great cost to the angel itself and the surrounding environment.. The angel suffers four points of aggravated damage ( possibly destroying the angel itself in the process) as the hive rips open and the whole swarm billows out in all directions, targeting everything in sight and detonating themselves with wanton abandon- attacking every living creature, object or structure within ten yards per dot of the angel's Rank and dealing it's damage rating in damage along with any of the missile's secondary effects. Naturally this function is never used frivolously, only angels on the verge of failing their Missions or near destruction ( often both at once) ever utilize these essentially suicidal method of revenge.<br /> <br /> Note: Angels that Fall with this Process still retain it, though the act of Falling seems to irreparably alter it's characteristics. The storage capacity is drastically lessened from 80 to 30 and the demon loses the ability to utilize the \u201ccarpet bombing\u201d feature. Other than that the Swarm Missile Hive functions normally, substituting Aether and Primium for Essence and Rank regarding costs and targeting options respectively. It should also be noted that the hive cannot be used as a Partial Transformation, the demon must assume full demonic form to access this ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-23-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:56:15-07:00","id":869395,"title":"","content":"Hey Guys! I have three more abilities for you guys, two more of them being demon/supernatural being hunting weapons ( since I have been on a weapon kick as of late) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I hope you enjoy them and let me know what you all think!<br /> ________<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Watchers' Eyes (Angelic Technology)</b><br /> Analysts are among the greatest tools the Machine has when it comes to surveillance and gathering information. And while nearly all Watchers possess many impressive Numina that bolster their ability to gather information and enhance their sensory range, the God-Machine understands that the ability to physically see multiple different locations at one time has it's merits as well. So it builds many of it's Eyes with the ability to use their own optics as removable biomechanical cameras- perfect tools to remotely keep their 'gaze' upon important targets without having to expend large amounts of Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel possesses a large number of eyes upon it's head. These eyes can vary widely in their appearance, from human like eyeballs with golden irises to metallic with camera lenses to glittering black spheres of glass with glowing pixels in place of irises or pupils. At any time these eyes can be pulled free from their sockets, biomechanical nerves and all, and placed upon virtually any surface \u2013 the nerves serving as living anchors.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel can remove any of it's eyes with a reflexive Finesse + Resistance roll and place them wherever it wishes. These removed optic organs function as video surveillance cameras that the angel can remotely view from with a Finesse roll, though they suffer a \u2013 1 penalty to noticing or reacting to nearby threats while remote viewing through one of their dislocated eyes. The angel may remove a number of eyes equal to their Rank, and each eye endures for a number of days equal to the angel's successes rolled or until they are destroyed- at which point they dissolve into a mixture of oil and blood that evaporates seconds later. Destroyed eyes are capable of being regenerated within the corresponding socket at a cost of two Essence per eye, and the angel can prematurely choose to regenerate any missing eyeballs at a cost of one point of Essence, at which point the dislocated eyes dissolve as if they are destroyed. In addition, while all eyes are in their proper places the angel benefits from 360 degree vision and cannot be surprised by anything not using supernatural means of stealth to hide them. Naturally, it loses this advantage once it begins removing and placing it's eyes elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aether Eradication Prod ( Angelic Technology)</b><br /> Energy cannot be destroyed, though it can be changed from one form to another. The God-Machine understands this concept painfully well; after all the waste heat of It's processes is what fuels Its wayward servants. But as Below, so Above, and the great Machine has developed many ways of manipulating Aether into different forms- this relatively simple weapon being of most practical use to Its hunters. Some Destroyers are outfitted with prod like weapons that are able to change Aether into a different form upon contact with a demon, a form that is sadly unusable to the Unchained.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: One of the angel's limbs is a meter long weapon that resembles a heavily modified cattle-prod with black sparks crackling between it's prongs, or a metallic police baton wreathed in arcing, multi colored lightning.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel is able to spend a point a point of willpower to activate the prod, and for the remainder of the scene can attack targets with a Power + Rank roll against their defense and armor rating. If used on mortal or a non-demonic supernatural, the prod works like a powerful taser, inflicting the Stunned tilt for a number of turns equal to the Angel's Rank + 1, though they can be roused into action through another character making a Wits + Medicine roll by attempting to stimulate their bodies to a point of functionality. Upon a demon or other being that stores Aether in their system however, this weapon is more problematic. Upon a successful attack, the prod causes the demon in question to lose a number of Aether points equal to the angel's successes. The prod also inflicts the Stunned Tilt like with other beings, though it only lasts for the following turn as the demon's internal systems automatically act to reroute power to compensate for the debilitating loss of energy. In addition, while the prod's ability to strip away a demon's Aether points can be used successively each turn, it can only inflict the Stunned Tilt every other turn.<br /> <br /> Note: Demons can retain an altered version of this ability that causes angels to lose points of Essence in the form of Aether; which the demon can harvest as normal- an added benefit of the angel being stunned for a turn, leaving them to recharge their own power stores in peace for a moment. The demon can use this weapon with a Dex+ Weaponry roll \u2013 the opponents defense should they be tangible. The stunning effect on other creatures works as normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Directed Energy Weapon ( Angelic Technology)</b><br /> It is said that all technological achievements are reflections of the God-Machine's esoteric grandeur. As humans make greater and greater leaps with their designs of their weaponry ( the laser weapon system onboard the USS Ponce being said to be a rather promising and more importantly inexpensive armament in comparison to the more traditional weapons she has.), one begins to see what the future may hold for warfare among the mortals. Some demons have found out first hand what it means where the God-Machine is concerned- far easier ways for Its loyalists to kill the Unchained and other enemies. While relatively new as far as in built form abilities go, having been first seen wielded by hunter angels only two centuries ago, the Directed Energy Weapon is still one of the more sophisticated weapon systems an angel ( or far more rarely a demon) can possess.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Built into the angel's forearm or mounted on one of his shoulders is a highly advanced projectile weapon that vaguely resembles a rifle or a cannon. The weapon itself is a marvel of technological achievement and it's aesthetics either accentuate or belie this sophistication; either being a geometrically flowing, artistically pleasing pulse weapon or a gritty, mean looking energy cannon of heavy industrial brutality, firing blindingly colorful bursts of energy at foes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The Directed Energy Weapon is a ranged weapon with a weapon rating of 5L and possesses a range of 80/100/300 that can be fired with a Power + Finesse roll while imposing a -2 penalty to initiative, and possesses three modes of fire- the first being a standard single shot burst, the second being a continuous stream of energy ( representing an autofire mode) and a semi solid blob of energy that explodes on contact, damaging objects and creatures in a three yard radius if they cannot make a dex+ Athletics roll to avoid the much slower projectile. In addition the Directed Energy Weapon is capable of inflicting lethal damage upon supernatural targets that normally take bashing damage from firearms. The weapon is powered by the angel's energy supplies; requiring the angel to spend a point Essence for every ten shots fired, two sustained beams, or three of the semi solid \u201cgrenades\u201d.<br /> <br /> Note: Demons can retain this Technology when they Fall, though it's damage rating is decreased by 1 and runs on Aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-23-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:57:26-07:00","id":869438,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> Thanks. (So many Form Gadget options...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T11:07:48-07:00","id":869444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=869438#post869438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> Thanks. (So many Form Gadget options...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Always happy to provide stuff to inspire others!<br /> <br /> And yeah, these open up quite a few more possibilities don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:14:08-07:00","id":870616,"title":"","content":"Here are three more for you guys!! ( I think for awhile I'll just be posting them in groups of three; that way it is easier for people to read without being utterly swamped by text.) I am eager to hear your suggestions on them! Also a minor thing to add is that designing Propulsions freaking suuucks- It's hard to come up with interesting and fun ways to move when the core already has so many... and unlike others, its harder to make alternate versions for existing ones... much less making new Propulsions hole cloth like th three I have designed ( and those probably will be the only three I design- though I do have ideas for an angelic version of Wings and Plasma Drive)<br /> ______<br /> <br /> <b>Jump-jets (Angelic Propulsion)</b><br /> When one hears the word \u201cangel\u201d, invariably images of radiant, terribly beautiful and horrifying inhuman beings descending from above on great wings come to mind. Unfortunately not all angels of the God-Machine are graced with the ability to fly, but to compensate for this earth-bound servants of the machine are often capable of incredible feats of mobility and agility. Angels with this form ability may not be able to soar among the clouds, but they can rule atop skylines and nimbly move about the cities of man with a fluid grace that more than makes up for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel possesses several thrusters on it's back and legs, which neatly seal themselves when not in use to prevent dirt and other particulates from clogging them.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel is capable spending a point of Essence in order to quadruple their vertical jumping distance and quintupling their horizontal jumping distance. In addition, should the angel find themselves falling from a great distance they can spend Essence points in order to perform either short bursts or a continuous burn with their Jump-jets to slow their descent, lessening potential damage taken from the fall by one point per Essence expended in this manner to a minimum of 1 point of damage taken from said fall. Finally, this Propulsion can be used to give boosts to unassisted leaps, essentially allowing them to \u201c jump\u201d while in mid air- essentially allowing them to re-roll a failed jump reflexively, though this safety feature can only be used once per turn.<br /> <br /> Note: This Propulsion can be retained by demons, where its jumping distance modifiers are reduced by one, and is powered through Aether.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Early Warning System (Angelic Modification)</b><br /> Danger hides behind every corner and within every shadow in the World of Darkness, just waiting to reach out and inflict tragedy upon the unsuspecting- especially the unsuspecting. It is the job of many Guardians to be ready for when it does, to stand between the horrors of the night and those they are sent to protect, so the God-Machines grants them the tools needed to prepare for the worst before it truly happens.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel's body plays host to a number of early warning devices. The appearance of these devices can be something as artificial as an array of motion sensors to tiny biomechanical creatures that resemble diminutive birds that squawk and move their tiny wings in alarm in response to danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The Early Warning System adds a + 5 to the angel in questions' Initiative score and grants a + 3 to Perception rolls made by the angel. In addition, these sensory devices or creatures alert the angel should a potential enemy attempt to sneak up on or attack the angel from behind, rendering the angel immune to surprise attacks from behind \u2013 though supernatural powers that enhance stealth or render the enemy otherwise undetectable are still able to function at a \u2013 2 penalty.<br /> <br /> Note: This ability is also available to demons, and remains unchanged.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Faith (Angelic Process)</b><br /> The enemies of the Machine are legion, and while on an individual scale few ever are a match for it's servants in direct combat the foes of God are crafty and employ many tools of war to bring the loyal angels low. Fortunately the God-Machine has long since designed ways to defend against such forces, and its greatest warriors possess mighty shields to turn aside the burning metal arrows of the Unchained.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The angel has several metallic studs embedded in its shoulders, chest, forearms, legs, and along its spine. Should a metallic weapon or electrical charge strike the angel a nimbus of golden energy flares into existence for a brief moment as it nullifies the attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b>: The angel possesses a electromagnetic shield generator that renders it completely immune to electricity in any form, be it natural or supernatural, this includes form abilities such as Electromagnetic Pulse and Electric Jolt. In addition, this energy shield provides less impervious, but still mighty defense against weapons and projectiles composed of metal, granting five points of armor against metal melee weapons and complete immunity from firearms whose caliber is smaller than .50- these rounds simply are harmlessly deflected away from the angel's body regardless of the distance of the shooter. Naturally weapons that are not made of metal, that use unorthodox ammunition ( such as the Hod Rounds of Task Force: Valkyrie) or are of a high enough grade of ordinance ( such as the forementioned .50 caliber weapon or something even more powerful; a tank shell for example.) are not impeded by the Shield of Faith.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-23-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:30:38-07:00","id":870881,"title":"","content":"Do you think you could format these a little? Bold and/or Underline the names, with something done about Appearance and Mechanics? They kind of blend together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:55:52-07:00","id":871927,"title":"","content":"I 'll see what I can do tomorrow, my phone makes work like that nearly impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:02:51-07:00","id":872283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=871927#post871927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I 'll see what I can do tomorrow, my phone makes work like that nearly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can sympathize. If you want (and I get time) I could copy and format these to a doc and then send it to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:26:42-07:00","id":872290,"title":"","content":"I'd appreciate it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:27:21-07:00","id":873774,"title":"","content":"As I have exhausted my immediate ideas on form abilities ( having already designed near twenty six of them so far lol) and have not yet found anymore aside from Wings, which I will probably post later once I finish fixing it.. why don't you guys give me suggestions for pieces of occult technology to slap onto angels? Just post them and I will do my best to build something based on your initial concept. I think that will be fun, and I would love to see your suggestions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:46:00-07:00","id":874237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=873774#post873774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I have exhausted my immediate ideas on form abilities ( having already designed near twenty six of them so far lol) and have not yet found anymore aside from Wings, which I will probably post later once I finish fixing it.. why don't you guys give me suggestions for pieces of occult technology to slap onto angels? Just post them and I will do my best to build something based on your initial concept. I think that will be fun, and I would love to see your suggestions!</div> </div> </div> </div> How about an ability for transferring minds to artificial bodies and/or virtual realities? This can be used as a fail-safe for very important individuals, a reward or enhanced interrogation. It would probably be a Process. The mechanics should include a way for the mind to break free. I suggest that the mind has to find a Linchpin.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All these Angelic Form advantages are super cool and terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-25-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:36:30-07:00","id":874489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=874237#post874237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How about an ability for transferring minds to artificial bodies and/or virtual realities? This can be used as a fail-safe for very important individuals, a reward or enhanced interrogation. It would probably be a Process. The mechanics should include a way for the mind to break free. I suggest that the mind has to find a Linchpin.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All these Angelic Form advantages are super cool and terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... That could work. I already have an idea brewing. I'll see what I can come up with.<br /> <br /> Also; Thanks, I try my best!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:52:16-07:00","id":874533,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about one that grants bonuses against enemies that attacked the Angel the previous turn? Identifying vulnerabilities in their technique, following projectile trajectories back to their sources, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, I copied and formatted the entries here into a Google Doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O_HIomzEMusF-3-0KCWuaZh_KWhkC959745mF4-tWQw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a> (Maybe copy this to the initial post for easy reference?)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> PM your gmail and I'll just pass edit/ownership over to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-26-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:04:08-07:00","id":874541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=874533#post874533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What about one that grants bonuses against enemies that attacked the Angel the previous turn? Identifying vulnerabilities in their technique, following projectile trajectories back to their sources, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, I copied and formatted the entries here into a Google Doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O_HIomzEMusF-3-0KCWuaZh_KWhkC959745mF4-tWQw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a> (Maybe copy this to the initial post for easy reference?)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> PM your gmail and I'll just pass edit/ownership over to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that is something I could easily write up! In theory at least XD<br /> <br /> and I approve, it looks so professional! Medichanic Tools is spelled as Mechanic.. but not that big of an issue. easily fixed I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:12:58-07:00","id":874549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=874541#post874541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that is something I could easily write up! In theory at least XD<br /> <br /> and I approve, it looks so professional! Medichanic Tools is spelled as Mechanic.. but not that big of an issue. easily fixed I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I thought that was a typo, so I &quot;corrected&quot; it while moving things around. Feel free to change it to what it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:18:55-07:00","id":874554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=874549#post874549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I thought that was a typo, so I &quot;corrected&quot; it while moving things around. Feel free to change it to what it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep it is a portmanteau of Medic and Mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:58:42-07:00","id":874688,"title":"","content":"Well here is the targeting aid first!<br /> <br /> ____<br /> <br /> <b>Retroactive Targeting System ( Angelic Technology)</b><br /> The God-Machine is omnipresent; it's superstructure ( and Infrastructure) existing throughout the world past, present, and future. Angels are likewise quantumly stable, and a number of Guardians or dedicated hunter-angels are equipped with the hardware to analyze damage inflicted to their structure by previous attacks in order to predict future hostile actions with progressive aptitude- scanning enemy body stances, calculating the impact velocity and trajectory of projectiles, and other more esoteric methods of occult analysis.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The angel possesses a third eye upon their forehead. While the eye can resemble almost any mechanical or biological optic sensor, all of them seem to possess a thousand yard stare, only focusing in on objects should the angel be injured.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> Should the angel suffer a point of damage due to being the target of a hostile character the technology reflexively activates, granting a + 2 bonus to combat rolls against that target, which now benefit from the rote quality. In Addition, this Technology also functions in response to projectile weapons such as firearms; upon being wounded by a successful firearms attack roll the angel is then able to apply it's defense against future firearm attacks by that user, as well as gaining a + 1 to it's defense against said user. Subsequent wounds inflicted by opponents impart an additional + 1 bonus to the angel's defense and combat rolls, capping a + 5 for both modifiers. It should be noted that these bonuses only apply to the opponents who wound the angel ( ex. Jimbob has shot Exampiel twice, thus she has a + 3 to her combat rolls and + 2 to her defense against Jimbob, but she has no bonus modifiers against Jennysue, who has yet to attack her.).<br /> <br /> While this Technology can function against multiple opponents at once, the angel suffers a - 3 to their defense against opponents who have yet to wound the angel. Not only that, as the angel's defensive and offensive systems are so focused on targeting those who are already catalogued in the targeting matrix any damage inflicted is increased by one point ( an attack that does two damage would do three and so on). The trade off for this is once they <u>do</u> land a successful hit, the matrix then locks on to the new opponent as well, and the penalties are replaced with the bonuses described above.<br /> ____<br /> <br /> The mind transfer Process will be ready later, after I take care of rl stuff such as work and other things lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-30-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:04:27-07:00","id":878952,"title":"","content":"It took a bit longer, but I finally got around to creating the mind transference Process. I will confess this one was a bit more difficult to write due to it being more suitable to a Numen than a form ability, but I then got inspiration from another one of my favored role playing games and well.. here it is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ____<br /> <br /> <b>Cortical Stack-trap( Angelic Process)</b><br /> Humanity as a whole is obsessed with the concept of transcending their own mortality, in some form or another. Whether it is going to a paradise realm after they die or becoming one with the living universe or something as mundane as achieving immortality through the digitalization of one's consciousness - the desire to persist beyond the end of one's natural life is omnipresent. The God-Machine understands this desire to escape death all too well and has devised methods to exploit it that are legion, this Process being but one of them. With it an angelic servant is able to transfer the mind of a mortal into a cybernetic device born of his own biomechanical flesh, an ideal way to reward faithful servants with the promise of an immortal body.. or a trap for inglorious heretics from which there is nearly no chance for escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> At the base of the angel's skull is a triangular implant, which can be removed to reveal that the device is a small, biomechanical tetrahedron that pulses with a faint blue-white light.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> This ability is unusual as it relies on the angel to infuse it's own ephemeral flesh with a human momentarily in order to function. The angel removes his cortical stack-trap and inserts the device into the base of the target human's head with a Finesse+ Resistance roll - the target's stamina + defense ( if the target is resisting, if not the penalty is only their stamina), inflicting a single point of aggravated damage should the roll succeed as it enters the target's skull. Upon success the Angel rolls it's Power + Finesse + Rank - the target's Resolve + Composure ( if resisted), succeeding this subsequent roll the angel stores the target's mind within the device, which it may retrieve. This process leaves a biomechanical interface port behind where the initial wound was inflicted, allowing the mind to be re-transferred to it's original body should the angel choose. This device is surprisingly modular and can interface with most forms of machinery that is capable of accepting a data storage device, uploading the mortal's consciousness onto a digital medium for a variety of purposes- in which the mortal is then capable of manipulating whatever device they are uploaded to with the appropriate skill or attribute rolls ( As a rule, being a digital entity robs the character of being able to make use of most physical or attributes aside from Dexterity, since they no longer have a body. Exception occur when the character has access to a form that allows for interaction with the physical world- a piece of industrial machinery, a vehicle.. or a robotic drone body being some examples.)<br /> <br /> The target's own body falls into a state of suspended animation that to all the world resembles a coma, albeit one where the victim impossibly requires no sustenance to maintain the body's life functions. As long as the target's mind is separated from the body this suspended animation continues on, though the body is still very much mortal an can be killed - which forever destroys any chance the target's mind has of returning to an organic form ( well sort of, the cortical stack-trap could be inserted into another living body that has been the victim of this Process.. but that holds its own problems).<br /> <br /> These cortical stack-traps persist for as long as there is a consciousness within them, and the angel may generate new ones with an expenditure of a willpower point and five points of Essence. In addition, the angel may possess a number of active stack-traps in use equal to their Rank+ 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-30-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T15:06:13-07:00","id":890187,"title":"","content":"It's been awhile since I've added any new form abilities to this thread, rl matters and the werewolf stuff demanding the majority of my attention.. but I do have two new ones for those of you who enjoy this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Enjoy, and as always let me know what you think! Once again, there is another Modifcation that I sort of think is too powerful for a Modification.. yet at the same time it does what a Modification is supposed to do- amplify and exaggerate physical capabilities.<br /> <br /> ____<br /> <br /> <b>Reaper Life-Scythes ( Angelic Technology.) </b><br /> Sometimes the God-Machine requires living things to die in order to further a project; it is a simple, objective fact. This is achieved any number of ways; a family of four dying in a terrible premeditated car accident, a former angel is torn apart by packs of man-maggot things with steel edged mouthparts, or a loyal servant is merely cut into over and over again for hours- a long and agonizing death that requires an equal amount of the hapless mortal's life force and misery to power the appropriate Occult Matrix. Destroyers and Psychopomps armed with this form ability are terrifying harvesters who rip away the soul-sparks of those they kill- a remnant of that energy being left behind to lend vitality to the reapers responsible.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Reaper Life-Scythes come in many forms ranging from techno-organic Praying Mantis-like forelimbs to traditional rune-engraved scythe blades replacing the wielder's hands entirely to diseased, bony sickles extending from one's forearms.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> The Scythes are a 3L weapon with a -1 penalty to Initiative that are capable of inflicting lethal damage upon supernatural entities. These blades can also be partially retracted somewhat- becoming 2L weapons, losing their Initiative penalty in the process. In addition, the Scythes are designed to rip away the life energy of those they've wounded; every two points of damage inflicted by the Scythes the angel regains one point of corpus lost to lethal damage - though the Scythes cannot repair aggravated damage in this fashion.<br /> <br /> note: Demons can retain this form ability, and it is one of the very few that possesses even greater functionality than they did while still in direct connection with the God-Machine. No longer used to supply occult energies to the Machine, a Demon can make full use of the life harvesting powers of her scythes, regaining health on a 1:1 ratio with the damage she inflicts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Psionic Amplifier Nodes ( Angelic Modification)</b><br /> The brain is an incredible organ, it's potential is vast and it's complexity beautiful and mind numbing. Angels are an order of being higher than humans, so it stands to reason that their cognitive potential is even greater - shackled and constrained as it may be by the God-Machine. Sometimes though, the great Machine has use of such intellect and other more... physical benefits thereof. As such, Analysts are the most common angels to receive these enhancements in the sake of missions that require both tremendous processing power and, very unusual for Analysts, a means of interacting with their targets without making physical contact.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Angel has several external brains along its sides while it's own brain is exposed, though all of these neural nodes are protected by nearly unbreakable membranes of psychic force, shielding them from the elements of the outside world.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> This Modification grants the angel a staggering +5 to rolls related to mental tasks, and grants him enough cognitive focus to perform two actions in a single turn, so long as they are separate actions ( such as performing a non combat action and a combat action). In addition, this grants the ability of telekinesis that functions much like the Telekinesis supernatural Merit, albeit with a +2 modifier regarding it's use.<br /> <br /> Note: Demons can retain this ability, though it's modifier for Intelligence rolls is reduced by one, and it loses the ability to perform two actions at once. It keeps it's telekinetic properties however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:26:05-07:00","id":897780,"title":"","content":"Was brainstorming Style ideas that would take Demonic Form into account. I was thinking of one based around the various ranged weapons abilities and thought &quot;maybe some power to graft/integrate another weapon into your body might be nice&quot;. Couldn't figure out how to fit it in to make sense. I know you can subsume Gadgets (via the Merit), but I'm not sure that will let you use an Embedded Flamethrower as simply a Flamethrower (for example). Might there be a niche for a kind of &quot;placeholder&quot; Technology, where you can integrate any normal weapon you might encounter and use that as if it were a Form ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:42:51-07:00","id":897794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=897780#post897780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was brainstorming Style ideas that would take Demonic Form into account. I was thinking of one based around the various ranged weapons abilities and thought &quot;maybe some power to graft/integrate another weapon into your body might be nice&quot;. Couldn't figure out how to fit it in to make sense. I know you can subsume Gadgets (via the Merit), but I'm not sure that will let you use an Embedded Flamethrower as simply a Flamethrower (for example). Might there be a niche for a kind of &quot;placeholder&quot; Technology, where you can integrate any normal weapon you might encounter and use that as if it were a Form ability?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll see what I can come up with bud, it sounds like a pretty interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:46:08-07:00","id":897854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=897794#post897794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll see what I can come up with bud, it sounds like a pretty interesting idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Because while the current selection of &quot;weapon&quot; Form Abilities is nice, something like this could allow for far more options without having to write up a new Form Ability for each one. And, thinking about it further, the ability to integrate current weaponry seems like the kind of efficiency the Machine would approve of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:08:47-07:00","id":897930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=897854#post897854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. Because while the current selection of &quot;weapon&quot; Form Abilities is nice, something like this could allow for far more options without having to write up a new Form Ability for each one. And, thinking about it further, the ability to integrate current weaponry seems like the kind of efficiency the Machine would approve of.</div> </div> </div> </div>agreed, in fact I think such a form ability would be quite common for heavy combat oriented Destroyers ( which is amusingly ironic now that I've wrote this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:22:52-07:00","id":897947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=897930#post897930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> agreed, in fact I think such a form ability would be quite common for heavy combat oriented Destroyers ( which is amusingly ironic now that I've wrote this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sneaky ones too - anyone shot by the Form Ability was shot by the weapon that was integrated, so if you need it to look like a specific type of weapon killed someone (for casting blame or inducing paranoia), you can have a Destroyer with Phasing integrate a distinct weapon, Phase into the room with the target, kill them, then Phase out and leave the scene. Investigators will find they were shot by Weapon XYZ.<br /> <br /> And if the form is inherently modular (in that the Angel/Demon can drop the weapon at any time to integrate a new one), it lets them reconfigure their weapon's load at a moments notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:36:20-07:00","id":897960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=897947#post897947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sneaky ones too - anyone shot by the Form Ability was shot by the weapon that was integrated, so if you need it to look like a specific type of weapon killed someone (for casting blame or inducing paranoia), you can have a Destroyer with Phasing integrate a distinct weapon, Phase into the room with the target, kill them, then Phase out and leave the scene. Investigators will find they were shot by Weapon XYZ.<br /> <br /> And if the form is inherently modular (in that the Angel/Demon can drop the weapon at any time to integrate a new one), it lets them reconfigure their weapon's load at a moments notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always useful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T15:11:04-07:00","id":917000,"title":"","content":"Here you are Vent0, sorry it took so long! I hope you like it!.<br /> <br /> ____________<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon Integration System (Angelic Modification)</b><br /> Many angels are built or grown with a variety of &quot; natural&quot; weapons; some more esoteric than others. Sometimes, however, the situation at hand calls for a more mundane approach when it comes to the art of killing, or at times requires an unwitting pawn's handgun in order to implicate them in a murder for a specific Occult Matrix to fully actualize. Those angels with this ability are able to incorporate mortal weaponry into their biomechanical forms, utilizing these devices as fluidly as they can their own angelic abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The angel has several ports along it's body. When incorporating a mortal weapon a host of biomechanical nerves and wires emerge from a port and forcibly invade the material structure of the weapon as they anchor it inside the port, shifting it to a bio-ephemeral state for the duration of the merger.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> The user of this ability is capable of merging a non-supernatural weapon into their angelic form by rolling Finesse + Resistance and spending a number of points of Essence equal to the object's size. Once merged said weapon essentially functions as a form ability and the user can operate the weapon with a +3 bonus due to this more intimate connection, though the angel in question can only possess a number of these &quot;form abilities&quot; equal to half their Rank ( so one if Exampiel is Rank 1, two if Rank 4 and so on.). The weapons can remain merged with the user's body for a number of days equal to Rank before their biomechanical form rejects the foreign objects, ejecting them back into the world as if they were never part of the angel's form to begin with,- with an expenditure of a point of Essence the angel may retain the object for an additional day.however( though some rumors exist that particularly powerful angels leave a piece of themselves within these weapons should they be bonded to said angel for long enough- creating supernaturally enhanced tools.. but this has never been verified.). Lastly the angel may remove the weapon from their form at any time with a Finesse + Resistance roll and a point of Essence.<br /> <br /> Note: This ability can be retained by demons, though they can only integrate two weapons into their Demonic Forms, and may only retain these &quot;form abilities&quot; for a number of days equal to Premium, with the rule of spending Essence to extend the duration being replaced with Aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 06-18-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T17:07:03-07:00","id":917048,"title":"","content":"Nice, though I'm wondering why the limitations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:43:46-07:00","id":917108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=917048#post917048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice, though I'm wondering why the limitations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Balancing mostly, angels with their Influences, Manifestations, Numina, Incepts and ( if used in ones game, though they could be simply used as numina... as much as I dislike that solution) Form Abilities make for hellishly ( pun intended) formidable creatures, putting ten mortal machine guns, a half dozen grenade launchers, a pair of Stinger SAMs, and an 20mm anti-tank gun on top of all that is going beyond fearsome and into utter ridiculous ness.<br /> <br /> I'm all for making angels terrifying and nightmarishly strong, but there has to be a line somewhere, thus the limit on how many guns/swords/etc you can ductape to the thing xD.<br /> <br /> For demons its much the same, though they have to contend with the problem of also being fully material, and having to deal with things like weight and stuff lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 06-18-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:24:03-07:00","id":917130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=917108#post917108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Balancing mostly, angels with their Influences, Manifestations, Numina, Incepts and ( if used in ones game, though they could be simply used as numina... as much as I dislike that solution) Form Abilities make for hellishly ( pun intended) formidable creatures, putting ten mortal machine guns, a half dozen grenade launchers, a pair of Stinger SAMs, and an 20mm anti-tank gun on top of all that is going beyond fearsome and into utter ridiculous ness.<br /> <br /> I'm all for making angels terrifying and nightmarishly strong, but there has to be a line somewhere, thus the limit on how many guns/swords/etc you can ductape to the thing xD.<br /> <br /> For demons its much the same, though they have to contend with the problem of also being fully material, and having to deal with things like weight and stuff lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more why is there the time limit on incorporation. I was thinking something along the lines of capping it at one weapon at a time. Main benefits being &quot;Modular&quot;, &quot;Treated as full Form ability&quot;, &quot;Can't be independently targeted (see Form Ability)&quot;, &quot;Perfect copy (for implication)&quot;, and &quot;Infinite Ammo (like Rivet Gun)&quot;. <i>Maybe</i> some other boost (like the +3 you have, or Armory/Hurt Locker ammo modifiers). Just something to let an Angel/Demon have more weapon-based Form Abilities without writing up a new one per.<br /> <br /> Also, with Subsumed Gadgets, a Demon <i>can</i> &quot;duct tap&quot; a crazy number of weapons to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T05:46:03-07:00","id":917301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=917130#post917130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant more why is there the time limit on incorporation. I was thinking something along the lines of capping it at one weapon at a time. Main benefits being &quot;Modular&quot;, &quot;Treated as full Form ability&quot;, &quot;Can't be independently targeted (see Form Ability)&quot;, &quot;Perfect copy (for implication)&quot;, and &quot;Infinite Ammo (like Rivet Gun)&quot;. <i>Maybe</i> some other boost (like the +3 you have, or Armory/Hurt Locker ammo modifiers). Just something to let an Angel/Demon have more weapon-based Form Abilities without writing up a new one per.<br /> <br /> Also, with Subsumed Gadgets, a Demon <i>can</i> &quot;duct tap&quot; a crazy number of weapons to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually quite simple to- though they are integrated into the angel or demon s' body and act as proxy form abilities, they are still mundane weapons. The time limit represents the angelic or demonic form rejecting the weapons somewhat like how a body rejects an incompatible organ.<br /> <br /> And yes, demons can have buttloads of implanted Gadgets- though at nearly carastrophic costs to Cover. Having said that, they are still pieces of occult technology and there fore &quot;compatible&quot; with a Demon's body/demonic form.<br /> <br /> But if you want those sort of advantages, you are absolutely free to include them, I have no problem with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T20:12:04-07:00","id":919477,"title":"","content":"Thought on something that is more useful to a Demon, but an Angel still might find a use for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Dominion Processor</b> <b>(Angelic Process)</b><br /> Angels already are granted control over various aspects of reality related to their mission. There are situations, however, where a broader range of control is warranted. In these cases, the God-Machine equips Its Angels with additional reality manipulation engines, above and beyond what they normally have access to.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Angel has an obvious external processor that flickers with some representation of the force it manipulates when it is used.<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> The Angel gain access to another Influence with a rating equal to their Rank without having to trade in Numina or Manifestations. It must be in a <u>single</u> Influence, and cannot be split between 2 or more. It is otherwise treated as any other Influence they possess.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Demons may retain this ability, fueling it with Aether as opposed to raw Essence, but it takes them time to restore it to full functionality. The Demon only has access to an effective Influence rating of half their Primum (round up). Additionally, using the Influence provokes a Compromise roll (though it gets a bonus if the Demon is using a lower Influence effect than what they are capable of - +1 per &quot;level&quot; lower than their maximum). Whenever a Demon increases their Primum, they can change what the Influence is for, if desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:48:26-07:00","id":930912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=919477#post919477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought on something that is more useful to a Demon, but an Angel still might find a use for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Dominion Processor</b> [Rename?] <b>(Angelic Process)</b><br /> Angels already are granted control over various aspects of reality related to their mission. There are situations, however, where a broader range of control is warranted. In these cases, the God-Machine equips Its Angels with additional reality manipulation engines, above and beyond what they normally have access to.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Angel has an obvious external processor that flickers with some representation of the force it manipulates when it is used.<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> The Angel gain access to another Influence with a rating equal to their Rank without having to trade in Numina or Manifestations. It must be in a <u>single</u> Influence, and cannot be split between 2 or more. It is otherwise treated as any other Influence they possess.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Demons may retain this ability, fueling it with Aether as opposed to raw Essence, but it takes them time to restore it to full functionality. The Demon only have access to an effective Influence rating of half their Primum (round up). Whenever a Demon increases their Primum, they can change what the Influence is for, if desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I'm liking it. At the same time I think the use of the Influence should count as a Compromise roll, as that's altering the world in a blatantly angelic way, methinks the God-Machine would take notice and/or umbrage with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T11:26:28-07:00","id":930949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=930912#post930912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, I'm liking it. At the same time I think the use of the Influence should count as a Compromise roll, as that's altering the world in a blatantly angelic way, methinks the God-Machine would take notice and/or umbrage with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are already in Demonic Form, at least partially. Doesn't one cause fire to rain from the sky? Wouldn't that be attention calling too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:18:51-07:00","id":930976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=930949#post930949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they are already in Demonic Form, at least partially. Doesn't one cause fire to rain from the sky? Wouldn't that be attention calling too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I think when a Demon is using something like and Influence, that's interacting with the world in a way more in line with Exploits and Incepts in my opinion, so I think it should at least warrant a Compromise roll to see if the God-Machine's gaze would be more scrutinizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:02:30-07:00","id":931528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=930976#post930976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but I think when a Demon is using something like and Influence, that's interacting with the world in a way more in line with Exploits and Incepts in my opinion, so I think it should at least warrant a Compromise roll to see if the God-Machine's gaze would be more scrutinizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Updated the post. I added in a bit about there being a bonus to the Compromise roll if you are using lower effects than you are capable of (so if you have Influence 4, and you only use the default Strengthen, you get a +3 to the roll, but if you were to use Create (or a duration enhanced Strengthen), it would be a flat Compromise roll).","sig